ome/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:33:#   - The object vocabulary stays small: closed shell emitters, one L-shaped blocker, and at most no\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:278:    \"\"\"L-shape with a full right wall and a top bar placed outside the emitter's overlap rows.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:334:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with the legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/3/code.py:12:#      geometry is the L-shaped 4-cell walk that first travels 2 cells along the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/3/code.py:63:#        * geometry is unmistakably L-shaped knight motion instead of straight rays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/3/code.py:325:L-shaped walk with a dashed rhythm tied to the number of visible vertices.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/cf98881b.py:11:# The regions display a yellow pattern, a maroon pattern, and a blue pattern from left to right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/cf98881b.py:12:# To make the output, you have to copy the blue pattern first, then overlay the maroon pattern over that, finally overlay the yellow pattern over that as well.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/cf98881b.py:20:    - The left panel is yellow, the middle panel is maroon, and the right panel is blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/cf98881b.py:26:    - Overlay non-black maroon cells, then non-black yellow cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/cf98881b.py:29:    - Panel order encodes occlusion: blue is back, maroon is middle, and yellow is front.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/cf98881b.py:44:    # get the maroon pattern from the second section and overlay it on output grid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/cf98881b.py:45:    maroon_pattern = input_grid[:, red_bars_c[0] + 1 : red_bars_c[1]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/cf98881b.py:46:    output_grid = np.where(maroon_pattern != Color.BLACK, maroon_pattern, output_grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/cf98881b.py:48:    # output_grid = blit_sprite(output_grid, maroon_pattern, x=0, y=0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/cf98881b.py:68:    # make a maroon section and scatter maroon pixels in it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/cf98881b.py:69:    maroon_section = np.zeros((4,4), dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/cf98881b.py:72:        maroon_section[r, c] = Color.MAROON\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/cf98881b.py:81:    grid = np.concatenate([yellow_section, red_divider, maroon_section, red_divider, blue_section], axis=1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/43/code.py:13:#      bar above, a yellow bar below, a teal bar left, and a maroon bar right. The old rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:370:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with the legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/9/code.py:36:#      blue->orange, red->teal, green->maroon, yellow->black\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/25/code.py:36:#        red > teal > yellow > blue > maroon > grey\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/25/code.py:37:#      那么 9->red, 1->teal, 6->yellow, 2->blue, 8->maroon, 4->grey,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/25/code.py:39:#        (red, blue), (teal, maroon), (yellow, grey)。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/32/code.py:14:#    具体小例子：若输入里有 3 个红色 plus 顶点、3 个红色 dot 顶点、再加一小块蓝色 L 形噪声，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/32/code.py:38:#    marker 只用最规整的十字和单点；干扰项只用小 domino/L 形连通块；不同 patch 保持间距，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/10/code.py:303:    \"\"\"Build a non-emitter distractor sprite (C-shape, L-shape, or solid block).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/8/code.py:402:    - An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker is also fully embedded inside one stripe.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/8/code.py:409:    - A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: top-right corner means rotate 90 degrees counterclockwise, and top-left corner means rotate 90 degrees clockwise.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D5/2/code.py:21:#   * Difference: a red or maroon patch that sits in the reachable region no longer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D5/2/code.py:22:#     creates a temporary obstacle, and a hidden red/maroon patch is removed purely\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D5/2/code.py:34:#   blue, red, and maroon can coexist.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D5/2/code.py:49:# - A human can now see that blue pieces behave like rigid barriers while red/maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:383:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with a corner panel.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/1/code.py:410:    - An optional 5-cell L-shaped marker of color 9 sits inside one region and encodes a 90-degree rotation of the final output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D9/0/code.py:47:#    - The generator builds an outer L-shaped structural barrier that touches the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/24/code.py:24:#    Example trace: in the original puzzle a scattered green piece might be an L-shape with two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/3/code.py:12:    divider: still a full row / full column / L-shaped separator touching the border\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/3/code.py:390:    Repaint regions from L-shaped control markers, erase those markers, and optionally rotate the result using a color-9 L marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/11/code.py:302:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with the legend stack in one corner panel.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/33/code.py:35:#   - The legend still uses the original L-shaped border and sparse interior, so the task stays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/11/code.py:356:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D19/1/code.py:24:#    - new input: a 3-pixel L-shaped magenta marker at the same corner -> new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/11/code.py:19:#    maroon -> pink -> gray -> blue -> teal -> green. Example with three pieces:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/11/code.py:21:#    [maroon, pink, gray] confirm that same order after translation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/37/code.py:371:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/13/code.py:209:    - In that slid state, inspect each component's bbox and treat any background recess that reaches the inner face next to the separator as a trigger, even if the recess is open like a C-shape or L-shape, provided it is backed by a black right wall and also touches some other black edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D19/2/code.py:33:#     maroon(9)=paint the DOWN side\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D19/2/code.py:41:#   directly above it; with maroon symbol pixels it paints only the cells directly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D19/2/code.py:54:#   may contain red/green/yellow/maroon symbol pixels. The new solver therefore\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D19/2/code.py:150:    - Those embedded colors are the only instruction legend: red/green/yellow/maroon encode left/right/up/down painting for that whole wall component.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/11/code.py:9:#    - Fused: the legend is now a tiny 3-cell L-shaped component with no green border. It sits\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:46:#   L-shaped path whose vertical leg length equals the hole height.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:78:#   and the red signal is no longer a set of full-width rows but an L-shaped trace hugging the divider.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:87:#   stays legible even when multiple emitters contribute nearby L-shapes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/15/code.py:428:    Recolor boundary-marked regions by averaging palette positions, then optionally rotate with an L-shaped 9 marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/37/code.py:14:#   输入仍是 16x16 背景网格，左上角仍有 4x4 的 L 形 legend，其他对象仍是与背景 4-分离的多色矩形分量。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/37/code.py:28:#   * `_find_legend` 的左上角 L 形检测不变；legend 仍固定在左上，且内部仍是 3 个目标颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/37/code.py:56:    Detect the top-left L-shaped legend and return (size, border_color, interior_colors).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/32/code.py:375:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with the legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/20/code.py:71:# - The optional L-shaped color-9 marker is placed only inside one fragment and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/20/code.py:338:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/17/code.py:17:      legend display colors are {yellow, teal, maroon}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/17/code.py:19:      source task output would be [yellow, maroon, background]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/17/code.py:400:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/2/code.py:9:#      scraps, and an optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 rotation marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/2/code.py:346:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/32/code.py:35:#        to its right at clearly different distances. The farthest bar is maroon, then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/32/code.py:38:#        from the teal seed, in the order maroon -> orange -> blue -> green.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/16/code.py:359:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D1/0/code.py:38:#      collapse to a thin L-shape and make the task visually trivial.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/1b2d62fb.py:10:# In the input you will see two maroon bitmasks separated by a blue vertical bar\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/1b2d62fb.py:15:    Compute the logical NOR of two maroon masks separated by a blue bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/1b2d62fb.py:18:    - The input contains two same-sized maroon/black masks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/1b2d62fb.py:25:    - Output teal exactly where neither corresponding mask cell is maroon; output black elsewhere.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/1b2d62fb.py:49:    # create a pair of equally sized maroon bitmasks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/38/code.py:65:#   - _find_legend(...) from the source task assumed an L-shaped frame; that is invalid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/38/code.py:214:    - A straight color-3 separator line near the top-left acts as the legend divider instead of the original L-shaped frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/30/code.py:21:#      Fused output draws only the L-shape (top + right), and the shadow keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/10/code.py:319:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/2/code.py:25:#    - Small example: suppose a pink legend is an L-shaped ring with 2 holes. A grey\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/2/code.py:26:#      L-shaped sprite with 1 hole still matches because both fill to the same solid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/39/code.py:81:    In this combo, the border stays as an L-shaped frame but its size varies with the number of active colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/9/code.py:411:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/a2fd1cf0.py:11:    Draw a teal L-shaped path from the red pixel to the green pixel, moving horizontally first and then vertically.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/10/code.py:380:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with a legend line tucked into one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/4/code.py:526:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/24/code.py:19:   the hub's top edge is maroon, yellow still goes to the top because row order, not color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/21/code.py:460:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/2/code.py:48:#   {grey=5, pink=6, orange=7, teal=8, maroon=9}. This keeps connectors easy to isolate by eye.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/19/code.py:362:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/13/code.py:266:    - An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker may be embedded inside one region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/54d9e175.py:45:      blue->pink, red->orange, green->teal, yellow->maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/4/code.py:46:#    - Divider layouts remain full-row, full-column, or L-shaped, so the legend\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/4/code.py:387:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with the legend panel tucked into one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/23/code.py:338:    - There is no L-shaped rotation marker in this variant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/37/code.py:28:#    grey/orange/maroon. The output paints only blue/green/yellow hub sides; the red hub\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/5/code.py:339:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/78332cb0/D9/2/code.py:50:      an L-shape or left a cavity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/6/code.py:365:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/14/code.py:310:    - There is no separate L-shaped rotation sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/5/code.py:37:#   `_find_legend` 仍依赖左上 L 形边框；图例几何未改。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/36/code.py:344:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/28/code.py:31:     1. The legend is still a compact square with an L-shaped border, but it is pasted on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/28/code.py:29:        tall 5x4 -> maroon(9) / green(3)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/34/code.py:12:#      A maroon carrier rectangle containing accent pixels {8,5,2} is erased; a similar\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/34/code.py:56:#    - `main()` assumes the smallest top-left L-shaped border is the legend. The generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/23/code.py:10:# - D13/1 把“连接方向”从四联通边口扩展到 8 个方向。这里将对角连接具体化为 3 红像素的 L 形角口，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/23/code.py:44:#   斜向延伸的，因为端口是角落 L 形红口。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/e509e548.py:24:    - Count L-shaped 2x2 bend patterns across all rotations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/e509e548.py:46:        # Do this by building an L-shaped mask, and seeing how many times it appears in the sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/41/code.py:17:#    - 但图例不再是 4x4 的 L 形边框. 现在左上角是一个 7x7 的嵌套方框:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/41/code.py:34:#    - 图例尺寸固定为 7x7, 层数稳定, 视觉上明显不同于原题的 4x4 L 形角标.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/30/code.py:367:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with a legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/12/code.py:353:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/14/code.py:45:#      L-shaped legend border and its swatches stayed split into harmless fragments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/25/code.py:46:    - 模板仍沿整行或整列铺开，并贴住三条边；外部精灵只落在剩余的 L 形外区。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/8/code.py:28:#   a top-side legend [maroon, yellow] means a 2-piece chain with source order dark->light. If the two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/8/code.py:34:# - The legend uses only three fixed singleton marker colors: maroon / grey / yellow. Their luminance is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b0039139/8/code.py:34:#    D2-only would output the L-shape from the zero-mask crop. This combo instead fills\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/24/code.py:26:#    外部却没有同形状单片，而是两块颜色一致、都带缺角的 L 形片段；解题时要先看出两片可在\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/24/code.py:48:#    Only a few fixed dark->bright triples are used, such as maroon->orange->yellow or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/24/code.py:82:    (9, 7, 4),  # maroon -> orange -> yellow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/24/code.py:85:    (9, 5, 8),  # maroon -> grey -> teal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1045:    \"summary\": \"Triangular sprites emit maroon projectiles that travel along axis-aligned or diagonal paths, colliding to produce blue or recoloring opposing sprites to maroon.\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1047:    \"src\": \"triangular 3-pixel L-shaped sprites s\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1050:    \"path\": \"L-shaped sprites emit along diagonal from apex; V-shaped sprites emit along axis from apex; collision at 5 cells from apex\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1051:    \"trajectory\": \"paint maroon at collision point\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1052:    \"transform\": \"if projectile hits opposing sprite, recolor entire sprite to maroon; if two projectiles collide, paint blue at intersection\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1055:    \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify sprite orientation (axis-aligned vs diagonal) by checking pixel arrangement; Step 2: determine emission direction from apex; Step 3: cast ray from position 4 cells beyond apex; Step 4: on collision with another projectile path paint blue, on collision with opposing sprite recolor sprite to maroon\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1319:    \"src\": \"maroon pixels reachable from green square through orange background s\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1467:    \"transform\": \"decode the glyph into the orange phase tile; repeat that tile over the canvas; tile the glyph 2x2 at the center and recolor its foreground pixels maroon\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/3/code.py:28:#    - 小例子：某个输出洞里是一个 2x4 的双色 L 形 patch，但不同 piece 的内部朝向本身也会变化。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/3/code.py:35:#    - 所有 core 都用同一种非旋转对称的双色 L 形母板，但输出中的朝向会混合出现；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b0039139/3/code.py:36:#      section 3 = red(2), section 4 = maroon(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/11/code.py:29:#   single L-shaped leftover region. A sprite lying above or below the template is mirrored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/11/code.py:76:#    the output reads as a large L-shape plus a blocking vertical lane instead of a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/4c416de3.py:103:    - bg = most frequent color. Hollow 0-frames (possibly partial L-shapes); each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/2/code.py:32:    - suppose the bar has five colored notches: red, teal, yellow, maroon, grey\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:169:    Extend diagonal rays from L-shaped corner markers around hollow square rings on a checkerboard.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/6e453dd6.py:237:    \"\"\"Build a non-emitter distractor sprite (C-shape, L-shape, or solid block).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/16/code.py:24:#      L 形小槽。两个 3-dot 叶子虽然点数相同，但形状不同，只能分别插到左/右分支，最终得到\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/16/code.py:63:#      cavity；generator 让左叶对应 2x2 方槽，右叶对应 L 形槽来满足这一点。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:52:#     short outer glyphs are L-shaped instead of straight, and only the upward-facing Ls elongate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D11/1/code.py:48:- 交替色沿着单条直线/L 形路径分布，而不是散点分布，因此人类容易归纳“两色其实是一条墙”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/409aa875.py:25:    # L-shape (axis-aligned): one pixel has two 4-neighbors (the corner).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/409aa875.py:69:    Fire projectiles from 3-pixel triangle sprites; mark collisions with maroon or blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/409aa875.py:75:    - Each triangle has an apex and an emission direction determined by its shape: L-shapes fire diagonally away from the missing corner; V-shapes fire along the axis away from the open side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/409aa875.py:77:    - If it hits an existing sprite, that entire sprite is recolored to maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/409aa875.py:78:    - If two projectiles land on the same empty cell, that cell becomes blue (1); a lone projectile on empty bg paints maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/409aa875.py:80:    Key insight: The triangle's orientation encodes both direction and target; dual-projectile collisions on open bg produce blue, not maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/409aa875.py:116:    # Projectile hitting a sprite recolors the entire sprite to maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/409aa875.py:143:DIAG_DIRS = [(-1, -1), (-1, 1), (1, -1), (1, 1)]  # L-shape fires diagonally\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/409aa875.py:159:    Diagonal dir -> L-shape occupying 3 corners of a 2x2 (missing the corner opposite dir).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/21/code.py:92:#      is tied to a tiny fixed L-shape, while the terminal role is tied to a large\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/21897d95.py:255:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/21897d95.py:290:    - An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker triggers 90-degree rotation of the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/21897d95.py:297:    - A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: ┐ (corner top-right) → CCW 90°, ┌ (corner top-left) → CW 90°.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/6/code.py:51:    - 模板仍然占满整行或整列并贴三边，精灵仍只散布在 L 形外区。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:10:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:13:    - bg = orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:17:    - Maroon pixels connected to the destination through floor/maroon cells (not blocked by walls) are candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:19:    - Moved maroons are erased (replaced with floor color).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:21:    Key insight: Wall barriers restrict connectivity — only maroon pixels reachable via flood-fill through the floor qualify, so proximity alone isn't enough.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:49:    assert cand_ring, \"ring around destination must contain passable (non-maroon, non-red, non-wall) cells to infer floor color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:86:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:87:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:88:    maroons.sort()  # by distance then row then col\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:90:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:91:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:122:FILL_K_RANGE = (2, 9)            # how many maroon fill the dest block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:123:DISTRACTOR_MAX = 10               # max unreachable distractor maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:124:TOTAL_MAROON_RANGE = (4, 16)     # total maroon count bounds\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:265:    # Enforce total maroon count within bounds\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:281:    # Build INPUT: dest is green+red, maroon on source and distractor positions\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dd6b8c4b.py:286:    # Build expected OUTPUT: first k dest cells (row-major) become maroon, sources erased\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/f560132c.py:318:LEGEND_THRESHOLD = {8: 4, 10: 5, 12: 9}       # min extent threshold per side for legend L-shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/f560132c.py:320:LEGEND_ARM_RANGE = range(1, 4)                 # arm width/height options for L-shape construction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/f560132c.py:366:    \"\"\"Build an L-shaped legend piece mask anchored at (0,0) of the side*side grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/9385bd28.py:40:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/9385bd28.py:76:    - Scattered L-shaped corner markers of each marker color define opposite corners of axis-aligned rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/9385bd28.py:81:    - Determine which two bbox corners carry L-shaped anchors — the *other* diagonal defines the fill region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/9385bd28.py:86:    Key insight: The L-shaped anchors sit on the marker diagonal; the fill goes on the opposite diagonal of the bounding box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/cbebaa4b.py:265:    \"\"\"Draw an L-shaped path from *start* to *end*, preserving red (2) pixels.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/arc_utils.py:68:        (0x87, 0x0C, 0x25),  # 9 maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/19/code.py:11:#    - an L-shape with a missing bottom-right corner, or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:10:    - bg grid with monochrome 3-pixel L-shaped \"arrows\" (2x2 bbox missing one corner) and scattered colored wall pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/49/code.py:17:#       1. A 3x3 water block sits above a floating L-shaped source shelf. The right edge of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/19/code.py:42:#      repeated L-shaped local marks. That prevents the fusion from collapsing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/a6f40cea.py:545:    # Place L-shaped components in random corners\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D10/0/code.py:18:#     - 新逻辑例子：L 形 cavity -> ring = 围住 L 形每条外露正交边的单色壳层 -> solver 仍按同样方式找到该 bg 区域；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/7/code.py:59:#      become longer L-shaped paths; parity would create fake nodes on the arms. The fused solver\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/faa9f03d.py:456:    \"\"\"Build L-shaped arm waypoints for _path_crossing_all / _path_through.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D1/3/code.py:363:    \"\"\"Draw an L-shaped path from *start* to *end*, preserving connector pixels.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/18/code.py:106:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/18/code.py:287:    - Away from the legend, active marker colors appear as diagonal pairs of L-shaped corners; optional non-legend\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/27/code.py:34:#      are `A, B, C, D, X` where `A` is the largest L-shape and `X` is a distractor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/27/code.py:49:#    - The true anchor is uniquely largest and uses an asymmetric L-shape. That prevents\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/27/code.py:77:#    - The anchor L-shape often appears visibly rotated/flipped versus the output, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/eee78d87.py:41:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a 16x16 periodic lattice with the motif stamped in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/eee78d87.py:51:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/8/code.py:43:#    - The nearest piece to the strip is always the L-shaped anchor; the other three are pushed outside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/e3721c99.py:121:L_LAYOUT_MAX_SPAN = 24            # max legend line span for L-shaped layouts\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/e3721c99.py:280:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/3/code.py:174:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b9e38dc0.py:17:    Key insight: The wall endpoints define the opening direction; fill radiates outward through it, and obstacles block propagation along that same axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/7/code.py:388:LEGEND_THRESHOLD = {8: 4, 10: 5, 12: 9}       # min extent threshold per side for legend L-shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/7/code.py:390:LEGEND_ARM_RANGE = range(1, 4)                 # arm width/height options for L-shape construction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/7/code.py:436:    \"\"\"Build an L-shaped legend piece mask anchored at (0,0) of the side*side grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/17/code.py:189:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D12/0/code.py:330:    \"\"\"Draw an L-shaped path from *start* to *end*, preserving red (2) pixels.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/20/code.py:76:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/4/code.py:7:#   task: Identify a dihedral 20x20 motif placement from a masked L-shaped crop,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/4/code.py:8:#     then output the point-reflected L-shaped partner region instead of the full motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/4/code.py:16:#         sub-rectangle is replaced by a third mask color, leaving an L-shaped\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/4/code.py:20:#       output_content: the point-reflected counterpart of the input L-shaped region\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/4/code.py:40:#     - the fusion requires both at once: infer placement from an L-shaped sample,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/4/code.py:227:    Match a masked L-shaped motif crop and return the point-reflected L-shaped partner window.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/4/code.py:231:    - Two colors belong to the motif itself, while the third color fills one corner sub-rectangle so that only an L-shaped subset of the crop is visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/4/code.py:239:    - The masked corner tells you both which cells to ignore during recognition and how the non-rectangular viewport itself must move under center reflection, so solving the task means reflecting the entire L-shaped viewing region, not merely the visible pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/4/code.py:268:    then validates that the fused solver reconstructs the intended reflected L-shaped output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/43/code.py:24:#    - 小例子：区域内部是一个粗 L 形通道，黄色在左下角。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/2/code.py:115:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/26/code.py:28:      - fused behavior: in an L-shape moving right, a yellow in the short arm can step right only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/9/code.py:148:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/10/code.py:315:        assert info is not None, \"each marker component must be a 3-cell L-shape\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/10/code.py:372:    - Outside the legend, every marker color appears as 2-3 separate pairs of 3-cell L-shapes, where each intended pair shares either one row or one column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/29/code.py:19:#    with grey/orange interiors, one adjacent maroon head line, and one same-color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/21/code.py:31:        because a directed cross is not an L-shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/14/code.py:82:#       Grey means \"not flipped\" and maroon means \"flipped\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/14/code.py:88:#       1. Read the 2x2 hint block first. Example: a maroon square says the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D13/1/code.py:19:#      为了让 piece 在精确重合后仍保持 4 连通且不产生非红冲突，对角端口采用 3 红像素的 L 形角口；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D13/1/code.py:26:#      这里把对角连接具体化为角落 L 形红端口，使视觉差异稳定可见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D13/1/code.py:413:    \"\"\"Draw an L-shaped path from *start* to *end*, preserving red (2) pixels.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/4/code.py:432:    - Away from the legend, each marker color appears as one diagonal pair of L-shaped corner marks;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/18/code.py:12:     a 1-cell-thick maroon head line on one side, and a same-shaped maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/18/code.py:77:   - The no_head decoy leaves only one maroon line on its axis, avoiding marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D6/0/code.py:317:    \"\"\"Draw an L-shaped path from *start* to *end*, preserving red (2) pixels.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/25/code.py:19:#   再在黑框外找 maroon 线，并按“同色同形”找到 dest。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e39e9282.py:73:    \"\"\"Project maroon markers into adjacent grey or pink 3x3 squares, erasing grey squares afterward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e39e9282.py:76:    The grid has a dominant background, solid 3x3 grey and/or pink squares, and maroon marker pixels or segments directly touching one side of exactly one square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e39e9282.py:78:    Grey squares are erased; their adjacent maroon markers stay in place and stamp the nearest edge cell inside the grey square. Pink squares stay pink; their adjacent maroon markers disappear and stamp the corresponding cell on the square's middle row or middle column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/2/code.py:39:#    - blob 用小型 L 形 / 2x2 形状，既足够稳定，又能让“被撞到的格子”和“组件其余像素”同时可见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/13/code.py:130:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/f8f52ecc.py:117:    - Connect each consecutive pair by the shortest clear L-shaped path between the two components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/26/code.py:47:#   Original task: move NW by 3, recolor 3 grey cells, head stays maroon on destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/26/code.py:49:#   maroon, and because the destination is fully reached, turn the final 2-pixel head/destination pair\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/26/code.py:71:# - Original writeback assumed vacated cells become background and the final head always stays maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/26/code.py:85:#   row and column both change, the box leaves a maroon diagonal corridor, and a full contact turns the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/26/code.py:86:#   final marker pair black instead of maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/26/code.py:97:#   grey->orange by charge order, and maroon->black only on full docking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/23/code.py:138:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/27/code.py:9:#      black rectangular containers 0, striped orange/grey interiors 7/5, a maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/27/code.py:10:#      head line 9 attached to one side, and a matching maroon destination line on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/27/code.py:52:#    - Humans can see three coupled effects at once: motion toward the maroon target,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/27/code.py:64:#      maroon marks head/destination, and magenta is background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/22/code.py:121:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/fc10701f.py:21:    Move the orange rectangle onto the maroon rectangle and mark gated corridor crossings in red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/fc10701f.py:25:    - There is one solid orange rectangle and one solid maroon rectangle of the same size.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/fc10701f.py:30:    - Replace the maroon rectangle with the orange rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:19:# - The outer object is still a black rectangular frame with a full-edge maroon head line and an\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:20:#   aligned maroon destination line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/6/code.py:119:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/aaecdb9a.py:14:    palette: grey, red, teal, maroon, and pink. Objects are monochromatic\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/aaecdb9a.py:18:    For each palette color in order grey, red, teal, maroon, pink, count its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/18286ef8.py:18:    Use the pink control pixel to choose where the maroon pixel belongs inside the grey 3x3 region, and turn the control pixel maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/18286ef8.py:21:    - The grid contains one 3x3 region made from eight grey pixels and one maroon pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/18286ef8.py:25:    - Restore the old maroon cell in the 3x3 region to grey.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/18286ef8.py:27:    - Paint the selected cell maroon and recolor the pink control pixel maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/18286ef8.py:39:    assert guide_bbox is not None, \"missing grey/maroon guide region\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/18286ef8.py:46:    assert old.shape == (1, 2), f\"expected one maroon guide pixel, got {len(old)}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/18286ef8.py:171:    grid[cr0 + 1, cc0 + 1] = Color.MAROON  # initial maroon at center(1,1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/12/code.py:122:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/1/code.py:50:#    - No extra color mapping is introduced: maroon already denotes \"head/target\", and in the output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/1/code.py:51:#      the same maroon marks the traversed diagonal path. The only inference is that the vacated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/14/code.py:41:#      blue<->red, pink<->orange, teal<->maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/14/code.py:91:    8: 9,  # teal -> maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/14/code.py:92:    9: 8,  # maroon -> teal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D2/0/code.py:38:#    - Corner-triplet groups visibly become L-shapes instead of closed triangles,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/3/code.py:28:  grey/orange; a maroon head line attached to one side; an equal maroon destination line farther\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/3/code.py:72:- In the fused scene the maroon destination stays farther away, yet the output head stops before it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D11/2/code.py:28:#      L-shaped arrangement. It still contains red, but every attempted red-on-red translation\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:25:    assert len(directions) == 1, \"each moving object must touch maroon markers on exactly one side\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:45:    Push every colored object touching maroon markers straight outward until it reaches the grid edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:53:    - Clear each non-background, non-maroon object from its original position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:54:    - Translate it in the direction away from its maroon contact until the object reaches the grid boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:55:    - Keep the maroon marker pixels unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:58:    - The maroon contact side is a launcher: it determines a unique outward ray for the whole object, and the edge of the grid determines the translation distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:73:    assert 1 <= len(marker_components) <= 3, \"maroon markers must form 1-3 moderate components\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:74:    assert sum(int(comp[\"area\"]) for comp in marker_components) <= 17, \"maroon marker area must be moderate\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:75:    assert all(int(comp[\"area\"]) <= 9 for comp in marker_components), \"each maroon component must be moderate\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:123:# Canvas and maroon marker bounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:212:def _place_maroon_components(rng, grid, num_maroon):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:213:    \"\"\"Place separated maroon components; returns (components, occupied) or None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:215:    maroon_components = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:216:    all_maroon = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:217:    total_maroon = 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:219:    for idx in range(num_maroon):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:220:        remaining_components = num_maroon - idx - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:223:            MAROON_TOTAL_AREA_MAX - total_maroon - remaining_components,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:235:        placed = _try_place_maroon_component(rng, grid, cells, all_maroon)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:240:        maroon_components.append(placed)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:241:        all_maroon.update(placed)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:242:        total_maroon += size\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:244:    return maroon_components, all_maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:247:def _try_place_maroon_component(rng, grid, cells, all_maroon):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:257:        if any((r + dr, c + dc) in all_maroon for r, c in abs_cells for dr, dc in DIRS):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:263:def _available_slots(N, maroon_components, all_maroon):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:266:    for mi, m_cells in enumerate(maroon_components):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:271:                if 0 <= nr < N and 0 <= nc < N and (nr, nc) not in all_maroon:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:288:def _touching_maroon_sides(coords, all_maroon):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:292:            if (r + dr, c + dc) in all_maroon:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:328:    all_maroon,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:350:            if _touching_maroon_sides(inp_coords, all_maroon) != {(-dr, -dc)}:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:376:def _build_objects(rng, grid, all_maroon, chosen_slots):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:382:    input_occupied = set(all_maroon)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:397:            all_maroon,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:430:    num_maroon = rng.randint(MAROON_COMPONENT_MIN, MAROON_COMPONENT_MAX)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:431:    placed_markers = _place_maroon_components(rng, grid, num_maroon)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:434:    maroon_components, all_maroon = placed_markers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:436:    slots = _available_slots(N, maroon_components, all_maroon)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py:441:    built = _build_objects(rng, grid, all_maroon, chosen_slots)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D2/2/code.py:11:#    is (2,1) or (1,2). The filled path is the unique canonical \"2 then 1\" L-shape,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D2/2/code.py:42:#    repeated L-shaped bends. Because the input still only shows sparse vertices, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:25:# - The target is no longer a same-shape marker. It is a single maroon point placed farther ahead\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5e6bbc0b.py:42:    \"\"\"Compact the checkerboard's moving color toward the edge marked by the teal pixel, leaving a maroon swept trail on the marker line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5e6bbc0b.py:52:    - On the marker's row or column, color cells swept by shifted moving pixels maroon unless the final compacted line occupies them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5e6bbc0b.py:55:    The marker selects both the compression direction and the checkerboard color class that moves; maroon records the movement trail only along that marked line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d6e50e54.py:8:    \"\"\"Move each maroon marker toward the blue rectangle and recolor the rectangle red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d6e50e54.py:12:    maroon marker pixels. Each marker is horizontally or vertically aligned with the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d6e50e54.py:17:    maroon marker straight toward the rectangle along its row or column. Exactly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/17/code.py:42:       solids = [S1(blue), S2(maroon), S3(teal)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/17/code.py:45:       right top->bottom = [S1(blue), S2(maroon), S3(teal)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/17/code.py:47:       paired color swap -> frames use [blue, maroon, teal], solids use [red, green, yellow]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/17/code.py:48:       left bottom-up placement means top->bottom left becomes [F3(teal), F2(maroon), F1(blue)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/342dd610.py:25:      maroon, or blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/342dd610.py:29:    - Translate orange pixels up 2 cells, red pixels left 2 cells, maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/2/code.py:64:#     - 因为同一颜色会跨奇偶行重复，解题者能直接看到“上面这一行是 L 形，下面同色变成反向 L”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8618d23e.py:10:    Stagger the two horizontal input regions onto a larger maroon separator canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8618d23e.py:18:    - Create an output with one extra row and one extra column, filled with maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8618d23e.py:23:    The output is not a recoloring of either region; it inserts an L-shaped maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8618d23e.py:30:    assert not bool(np.any(g == Color.MAROON)), \"maroon is reserved for the inserted separator\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/cc9053aa.py:59:    \"\"\"Recolor the unique safe route between the two maroon endpoints from teal to maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/cc9053aa.py:62:    - A black background contains a teal 4-connected track, exactly two maroon endpoint pixels, and one or more orange blocker pixels embedded near the track.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/cc9053aa.py:66:    - In the remaining teal/maroon track graph, there is exactly one simple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/cc9053aa.py:67:      4-connected path between the maroon endpoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/cc9053aa.py:68:    - Recolor teal pixels on that path to maroon; leave endpoints, blockers, and all other cells unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/16/code.py:11:#   A 1-pixel black rectangular container had a maroon head line on one side and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/16/code.py:12:#   a same-shape maroon destination line farther away on the movement axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/16/code.py:15:#   1. The destination is no longer a line. It is a maroon L or T marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/16/code.py:43:# - A simple nearest maroon line match is unsafe: we must parse marker anchors and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/16/code.py:65:# - The maroon head and marker never touch in the input, so the two roles stay legible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/16/code.py:73:# - Every container has a full-edge 1-pixel maroon head adjacent to exactly one side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/16/code.py:74:# - Every destination marker is a separate maroon component analyzable as an L or T.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/9/code.py:26:# - D6/2: heads and targets are no longer globally maroon. Each mover uses its own visible marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/10/code.py:9:#      maroon head lines, and one maroon destination line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/58c02a16.py:24:    The solid L-shaped secondary-color border is a legend, not output content; it supplies the color used when the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:21:# - Outside the container there is now a 3x3 maroon arrow head plus a matching\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:22:#   3x3 maroon destination arrow further along the travel direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:33:#     * solver must infer R from the interior, then find the matching maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/22/code.py:34:#   if two station L-shapes meet at one corner, 4-connectivity yields two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/12/code.py:29:#    Example: with slot colors [blue, red, yellow, maroon] and input heights\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/24/code.py:15:#      这让输出从包裹式 V 形变成可预测的 A*O* 尖角 L 形。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/24/code.py:252:      yielding an A*O* L-shaped route instead of the original three-phase wrap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/963c33f8.py:86:    \"\"\"Drop the columns of the top marker downward, stopping blue-ended columns on grey obstacles and letting maroon-ended columns pass to the bottom.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/963c33f8.py:92:      are maroon and whose bottom row contains maroon or blue control pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/963c33f8.py:99:    - Contiguous maroon-ended columns pass through obstacles and bottom-align;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/963c33f8.py:102:    - When a maroon-ended drop lands through a grey bar on the bottom edge, clear\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/963c33f8.py:107:      \"stick to the first obstacle,\" while maroon cells mean \"fall through.\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/19/code.py:10:#   black rectangular containers, grey/orange interiors, and a maroon head line\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/19/code.py:11:#   with an aligned maroon destination line farther along the movement axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/5/code.py:9:#   maroon head line on one side, aligned maroon destination line further along the motion axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/14/code.py:70:  - The legend visibly shows an L-shaped offset, so the human can infer the move is not a straight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/14/code.py:387:      positions, so the legend encodes an exact L-shaped move rather than a unit direction sign.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/17/code.py:13:#     - D12 把原来的直 bar 改成 L 形 bar：一条贴边法向的主干加一条较短的侧向短臂。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/17/code.py:15:#     - 因而 solver 不能再通过“边界那头直线的内端 terminal”定位 segment，只能先识别 L 形结构，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/17/code.py:307:    Re-route each rope-like segment from the elbow of an L-shaped bar so it wraps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/17/code.py:311:    - Non-background objects come in triples: an L-shaped bar whose long stem is perpendicular to one grid edge, an irregular 1-cell-thick segment, and a nearby obstacle sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/28/code.py:8:# - The grid contains one clean lane of 2-4 same-direction containers and one shared maroon destination line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/54dc2872.py:52:    \"\"\"Move each marked L-shaped sprite onto the separate pixel matching its marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/ad173014.py:246:    \"\"\"Find an L-shaped path (0-2 turns) from start to end avoiding occupied cells.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/46/code.py:48:#    - L-shaped legends leave their interior bbox mostly background, but because the path touches\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/46/code.py:301:    - Exactly one border-touching legend appears in a corner as a thin strip or L-shaped path.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/2/code.py:10:#      也就是“斜向靠近 + 贴边前进 + 沿根侧正交退出”的 L 形；着色层则只保留 route 的第 1、3、5... 格。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/2/code.py:14:#    - 差异因此不是“先 L 再虚线”两件孤立的事，而是 solver 必须先恢复完整 L 形 corridor，之后才能在正确的几何顺序上做隔格采样。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/2/code.py:23:#    - 原 solver 的单调性断言是 FL*F*FR* / FR*F*FL*；融合后应改成 A*F*O*，否则会把合法 L 形错判掉。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/2/code.py:482:    Re-route each terminal-attached irregular segment around the nearest obstacle with an L-shaped wrap, then paint only every other cell of that rerouted path.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/2/code.py:490:    - Keep the full rerouted corridor only as an internal route; the visible output paints just route cells 1, 3, 5, ... in order, so the segment becomes a dashed L-shaped wrap with ceil(L/2) painted cells when the full route has length L.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/2/code.py:493:    - Solving the puzzle requires combining two cues at once: recover the hidden full L-shaped rope geometry around the obstacle, then apply a deterministic odd-index sampling rule to that route instead of painting it solid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8dab14c2.py:198:# Clean L-shape arm bounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e45ef808.py:40:    - Find the column whose first terrain row is latest; it is unique and its upper fill run becomes maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e45ef808.py:56:    maroon_col = int(deepest_cols[0])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e45ef808.py:60:    assert maroon_col != yellow_col, \"highest and deepest columns must be different\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e45ef808.py:63:    out[1:deepest_start, maroon_col] = Color.MAROON\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/23/code.py:12:  one maroon head line on a border side, and one aligned maroon destination line farther\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/9f41bd9c.py:25:      maroon, stopping just before the final outer bottom support pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/7e4d4f7c.py:10:    Compress the L-shaped cue to three rows and add a pink copy of the top-row foreground mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/21/code.py:505:    Re-route one side of each U-shaped bridge after identifying which attachment point of an L-shaped border bar lies closer to the nearby obstacle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/21/code.py:508:    - Background plus 1-3 triples. Each triple contains an L-shaped bar touching exactly one grid edge, a 1-cell-thick U-shaped segment whose two endpoints attach to the bar's inner elbow-side and short-arm-side attachment cells, and a nearby obstacle sprite of a third color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/41ace6b5.py:21:      fill all lower cells in that column with maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/41ace6b5.py:35:    maroon = 9\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/41ace6b5.py:92:        out[gray_row + blue_height :, c] = maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/aaef0977.py:35:      through the cycle g