rkers and maroon 9-rects stay neutral. A solid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/26/code.py:50:#   disconnected subnetworks. Neutral grey/maroon markers remain sparse, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/26/code.py:257:    - Pipe cells use the same color as the token they transport, while grey 5-cells and maroon 9-rects remain neutral routing aids.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/12/code.py:9:#   rectangular container, grey/orange interior, one maroon head line adjacent to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/12/code.py:10:#   one edge, and one matching maroon destination line farther along the movement\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/12/code.py:21:#      maroon, creating a docking seam. Otherwise the moved head stays maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/12/code.py:23:#   original: clear old box/head -> paste moved box -> paste moved maroon head.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/12/code.py:26:#             moved maroon head.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/12/code.py:39:#   full reach -> black seam, partial reach -> maroon head.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/12/code.py:49:#   maroon. Both are broken by the fusion:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/12/code.py:68:#   lose the maroon head in favor of a black docking edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/12/code.py:82:#   maroon front line -> black happens only on visible contact with the destination;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/27/code.py:452:    Route paired tokens through a shortest-path maze whose crossings reflect and whose maroon gates rotate the delivered shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D9/0/code.py:24:#    with a maroon head line and a matching maroon destination line on the movement\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D6/1/code.py:19:#   old output: draw the L-shape in 2, draw the shifted copy in 7 only on bg cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/33/code.py:38:    plus one detached L-shaped noise blob elsewhere\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/33/code.py:44:    1. Reject the L-shape because its component does not fill its bbox.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D9/1/code.py:17:#   magenta background, each with a maroon head line and a matching maroon destination\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D9/1/code.py:71:#   panels containing only grey/orange readings, with no black borders, no maroon lines,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/18/code.py:67:- The group layout is limited to row / column / L-shape arrangements, which stays readable and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/1/code.py:275:    Flood a branching pipe graph from one endpoint token, with maroon rectangles turning the flow by reflection.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/1/code.py:287:    - The task is neither simple endpoint pairing nor shape copying in place. You must infer a branching reachability graph, then replace each maroon block's old straight-through semantics with the correct reflective face pairing before expanding the BFS frontier.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/11/code.py:272:    Route each endpoint token through a wire component whose maroon square may fan out into several exits.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/11/code.py:285:    - The original shape-complement rule still applies, but routing is no longer a permutation. The maroon square\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D2/0/code.py:11:#      and a maroon head line plus a same-shaped maroon destination line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D2/0/code.py:29:#    - Keep 2-4 containers, same rectangular geometry, same single maroon color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D2/0/code.py:41:#    - Head detection assumes the closest maroon pixels to a container are the head,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/29/code.py:296:      each is a scaled 3x3 L-shaped prototype.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/38/code.py:85:#   \"maroon < teal\" numerically; the secondary key is purely spatial.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/15/code.py:343:    - The dominant color is background. Other cells form teal/grey wire paths, optional maroon rectangular pass-through blocks, and colored 3x3 tokens placed two cells away from degree-1 wire endpoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D2/2/code.py:34:  containers with grey/orange interiors, a maroon head line attached to one side, and a same-shaped\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D2/2/code.py:35:  maroon destination line farther along the movement axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D2/2/code.py:68:  assumes the intended destination is the nearest same-shaped maroon component in front. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/20/code.py:25:#      orthogonal wire permutation and optional maroon 9-rect junctions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/20/code.py:470:    \"\"\"Attempt to replace a wire segment block with a maroon pass-through rectangle.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:354:    - Background cells surround a cyan pipe system with optional maroon 9-rect pass-through blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/1/code.py:15:#   rectangular containers, grey/orange interior, maroon head line adjacent to one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/1/code.py:16:#   border edge, matching maroon destination line farther along the same axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/1/code.py:21:#   the destination line\". In the original task, the moved head remains maroon and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/1/code.py:48:# - The original writeback assumed \"destination always stays maroon\" by copying the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/1/code.py:50:#   moved head in maroon. That assumption is no longer valid on the full-docking\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/1/code.py:65:# - On a full dock, the front maroon line disappears into a thick black front edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/1/code.py:67:# - On a partial move, the maroon head stays visible, giving the human contrast:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/1/code.py:68:#   \"sometimes it is still a maroon head, sometimes it turns into black when it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/1/code.py:79:#   only the fully reached head/destination line turns from maroon to black.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/1/code.py:143:    line is absorbed into the container as black border instead of remaining maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/10/code.py:14:#   A literal \"keep only the target quadrants\" crop would become an L-shape, which is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/3/code.py:43:#      input = black box, maroon head above it, maroon destination farther above\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/3/code.py:44:#      output = moved black box, more orange inside, moved maroon head, destination\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/3/code.py:47:#      input = same geometry, but line color may be blue/red/green/yellow/teal/maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/8/code.py:41:#     - Use a tiny library of asymmetric 3x3 logical motifs whose non-anchor colors form L-shapes,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/8/code.py:56:#       - Non-anchor color regions are connected L-shapes, not filled squares, so anchor detection is stable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D8/2/code.py:12:#     rectangular container, maroon head line flush with one side, matching maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/2/code.py:41:  2x5(area 10) -> 3x4(area 12), while the L-shape disappears completely.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/4/code.py:267:      diagonal swap bands, optional maroon pass-through rectangles on straight vertical subsegments, and colored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/4/code.py:275:    - A maroon rectangle still acts as a chamber that passes a wire straight through from one face to the opposite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/27/code.py:29:#    L 形或随机散点。为了让 D15 也稳定可见，生成器强制输出至少跨 2x2 个粗块，并且\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/5/code.py:15:#     - The visible TL patch is a 2x2 logical L-shape expanded into 2x2 solid blocks:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/5/code.py:45:#       Restricting the source to a 2x2 logical L-shape keeps the recursion interpretable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/5/code.py:69:#       cell in the base L-shape guarantees obvious gaps, so the result does not resemble plain scaling.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/5/code.py:340:    \"\"\"Create the fixed 2x2 L-shape source motif with two distinct non-red colors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/3/code.py:57:#    Human solvers can see the black box, a maroon head line, a separate maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/28/code.py:402:    \"\"\"Attempt to replace a wire segment block with a maroon pass-through rectangle.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:32:#     - 原题通过容器外侧相邻的 maroon 头线确定方向\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:35:#       而是在同一轴的两侧各放一个候选 maroon 目标线；轴由目标线对给出，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/4/code.py:34:#      bottom band: D=3x3 maroon, E=3x5 yellow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/4/code.py:37:#    global area sequence B(yellow), C(green), D(maroon), A(green), E(yellow).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/4/code.py:42:#      maroon block: D\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/5/code.py:17:#       本实现采用固定色序 [9, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3]，即 maroon -> orange -> pink -> grey -> yellow -> green。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/5/code.py:40:#    输入仍只有 L 形边线、统一背景和两排稀疏矩形。少量 minority 像素只放在矩形内部，既能强调“主体色”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/23/code.py:50:#    - 新增的 L 形仍然局限在原有 3x3 token 框里，没有引入更大物体；远端补形和本地残留都与导线分开\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/23/code.py:52:#    - 9-rect 仍然是规则矩形，而且只嵌在竖直线段里，便于人眼数出“这条路径经过了几个 maroon 块”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D16/0/code.py:28:    - Head and destination remain maroon full-edge lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/23/code.py:40:#   combo target input: a 3x3 red anchor plus a few stray teal/maroon pixels nearby.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/35/code.py:74:#   L-shaped \"three quadrants kept\" alternative that would be hard to parse.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/27/code.py:23:#            maroon sprite -> grey frame\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D16/1/code.py:20:     interiors, maroon head lines and matching maroon destination lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/15/code.py:41:#       Suppose TL input uses {orange anchor, teal, pink, maroon}; TR anchor is green,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D3/1/code.py:9:#   containers, gray interior cells, one 1-cell-thick maroon head line on a container side,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D3/1/code.py:10:#   and an aligned maroon destination line farther along the motion axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D3/2/code.py:64:  - 仍然只使用 magenta 背景、黑框容器、灰/橙内部和 maroon 标记，图面层次简单。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/18/code.py:18:#      A: sparse L-shape -> rotated sparse L-shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/25/code.py:31:#      test src: an L-shaped path\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/29/code.py:52:#       s3 blue L-shape empty\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/18/code.py:7:#   原题会把同对角线的一对蓝端点直接补成整条 45 度对角线；D1/1 把这一步改成固定方向的 L 形最短路。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/18/code.py:13:#   本融合版则只补到 (3,6) 为止，(5,6) 保持背景、(6,6) 仍是原始蓝端点，于是既能看见 L 形拐角，也能看见被品红截断的空尾巴。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/25/code.py:25:#      object share a visible geometric family: rectangle / L-shape / irregular.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/25/code.py:37:#      a 2-hole object with two L-shaped holes used to become one fixed teal ring with magenta\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/25/code.py:38:#      holes. In this combo it becomes the body color assigned to (2 holes, L-shape), while one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/25/code.py:286:      object's hole family as rectangle / L-shape / irregular, and recolor the whole object by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/3/code.py:28:#     - A full-edge maroon line still marks the movement direction, with an aligned maroon destination line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/8/code.py:45:#    - legend rows say red->blue, green->maroon, yellow->orange, teal->pink.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/8/code.py:48:#    - Combo output becomes [blue, maroon, orange, pink].\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/13/code.py:25:#        legend bottom row         = [maroon, blue, yellow]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/13/code.py:26:#        decoded map               = {yellow->maroon, red->blue, green->yellow}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/13/code.py:28:#        fused-variant output      = [blue, yellow, blue, maroon]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6ffbe589/7/code.py:79:#       clean L-shaped region where cues can sit without overlap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D15/2/code.py:67:#   black frames, grey/orange interior, and maroon markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D13/0/code.py:20:#    black-bordered rectangles, grey/orange interiors, one adjacent maroon head line,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D13/0/code.py:21:#    and one aligned maroon destination line on the movement axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/22/code.py:27:      H1 = 2x3 rectangle, H2 = L-shape, H3 = 2x2 rectangle, H4 = staircase\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/19/code.py:22:#   domino/L-shape rather than only a singleton pixel. The solver still matches only by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/3/code.py:64:#      the background away from yellow to maroon(9). This keeps all three hole bands visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D13/1/code.py:14:#     - a full-edge maroon head line sits next to one side of the container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D13/1/code.py:15:#     - an identical maroon destination line lies farther away on the same axis\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/17/code.py:17:#        src slot = 3x3 L-shaped color 7\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/17/code.py:23:#        src loses the L-shape and gains an outline-colored T-shape in the same slot bbox\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D13/3/code.py:11:#      containers, grey/orange interiors, and maroon head/destination lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/30/code.py:50:- Fill colors are restricted to orange/teal/maroon, so outline colors never appear as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/30/code.py:135:FILL_COLOR_CODES = [7, 8, 9]  # orange, teal, maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D13/2/code.py:19:#     - the head and destination are still identical maroon lines on the movement axis\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/20/code.py:47:- Fill colors are restricted to orange/teal/maroon, so outline colors never double as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/20/code.py:129:FILL_COLOR_CODES = [7, 8, 9]  # orange, teal, maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:68:#      1. blue L-shapes identify arrow tips and directions;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:379:    - The background is the most common color. Active blue objects are 3-cell L-shaped arrows; the degree-2 corner is the tip and the missing diagonal quadrant gives the arrow's facing direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D6/0/code.py:3:# Change: 1:1 — 每个容器恰好对应一条目标线，颜色相同（均为maroon/9）... → 多容器共享一条目标线 (many:1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/23/code.py:39:#       但这里三个黑框会连成一个 12x12 的 L 形大组件，灰框是一个单独 6x6 组件，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/28/code.py:12:#      L-shapes or a 3-cell T-like motif. That cue is NOT rotated; it encodes the payload's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/16/code.py:19:#      if a red L-shaped subsprite in src matches the upper-right dst hole, old output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/16/code.py:21:#      whole canvas, the dst hole still turns red, and the old red L-shape inside src\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/16/code.py:22:#      becomes a grey L-shape at the same absolute coordinates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D6/1/code.py:3:# Change: 1:1 — 每个容器恰好对应一条目标线，颜色相同（均为maroon/9）... → 一个容器对应多条目标线 (1:many)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D6/2/code.py:3:# Change: 1:1 — 每个容器恰好对应一条目标线，颜色相同（均为maroon/9）... → 颜色匹配配对\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D6/2/code.py:23:# - The only semantic change is that head/destination markers are no longer globally maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/18/code.py:544:    \"\"\"Build L-shaped arm waypoints for _path_crossing_all / _path_through.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D14/0/code.py:16:#       gray/orange interior, maroon head line and matching maroon destination line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new