:34:#      recolored according to the glyph color instead of always maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/1/code.py:44:#    black, and at most one case reuses maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/1/code.py:79:#    red(2)   -> phase (1,0), stamp maroon(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/1/code.py:81:#    No case matches the exact original behavior (zero shift + maroon stamp), so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/1/code.py:235:    # differ from maroon. With the current tables this is true for every color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c416de3/D3/2/code.py:151:#      from the corner. This forms a tiny inward L-shape on the border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/5/code.py:9:#    3x3 interior is now a two-color asymmetric motif such as an L-shape. After the move, the full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/3/code.py:28:#    - Recoloring all center glyph cells to maroon is invalid under D4/0; both layers must retain their original\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/23/code.py:34:#   strictly outside the frame bbox in the opening direction, keeping the scene non-overlapping and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:22:#     one centered 12x12 maroon stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:43:#   - maroon overwrite remains safe because only the centered stamp is recolored; the background lattice underneath is irrelevant\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:51:#   - only one compact maroon object is overlaid on the lattice, so the output remains readable despite the larger center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:53:#   - output colors stay {black, orange, maroon}; the fusion only changes shape construction, not palette complexity\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/11/code.py:141:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into the original per