etric rectangular lattice and stamp a maroon 2x2 copy at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/37/code.py:178:      orange, nor maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/37/code.py:187:      the original glyph as a centered 6x6 maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/7/code.py:129:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 rhombic lattice whose two diagonal axes use different periods, then stamp the motif in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/7/code.py:139:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and overwrite its true cells with maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/15/code.py:19:#      whole-rectangle reflection, then draw a 1-pixel-wide monochrome L-shaped trail from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/15/code.py:58:# - Trail paths are center-to-center L-shapes, so every trail stays in-bounds automatically once\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/15/code.py:437:    marker-colored L-shaped trails from each source piece to its reflected target box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D5/1/code.py:556:    \"\"\"Build L-shaped arm waypoints for _path_crossing_all / _path_through.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/42/code.py:21:#    same structure with 3-pixel bands. The center 6x6 maroon stamp stays unchanged,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/42/code.py:44:#    The lattice is still a single repeated background pattern plus one maroon center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/42/code.py:141:    - Fill the 16x16 output by tiling this expanded orange/black lattice, then stamp a 2x2 repetition of the input glyph in maroon inside the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/25/code.py:35:#    - The opening direction is inferred from structure geometry alone, then all slot\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/25/code.py:71:    \"\"\"Return one slot-anchor cell per lane for a candidate opening direction.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/25/code.py:195:    - Infer each structure's opening direction from the side that exposes several\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/25/code.py:197:    - For every slot lane, look straight outward along that opening direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/35/code.py:60:#      black/orange/maroon. Input colors only partition candidate objects from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/35/code.py:159:    Extract the repeated 3x3 contour code from a noisy 6x6 orange grid, then render the same 16x16 periodic lattice and central maroon stamp as in the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/35/code.py:169:    - Decode that mask into the period-3 orange/black tile, repeat it over the 16x16 canvas, then stamp a 2x2 maroon tiling of the glyph into the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/32/code.py:19:#         maroon 2x2 stamp of the original glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/32/code.py:34:#      7. The 6x6 maroon center stamp is still a 2x2 tiling of the input glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/32/code.py:39:#      the output becomes 11x22 before the centered 6x6 maroon H-stamp is added.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/32/code.py:73:#      maroon stamp. No extra markers are introduced.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/32/code.py:79:#    - Output still uses only black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/32/code.py:142:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a rectangular anisotropic lattice, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the output center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/32/code.py:152:    - Convert the coarse 3x3 phase tile into that rectangular period, tile it across an output whose height and width each use their own period formula, and then place a centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp of the original glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/27/code.py:20:#     - Warm-colored movable pieces come in exactly two visibly related shades: red and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/27/code.py:62:#     - The shade cue is purely visual: red versus maroon component counts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/17/code.py:14:      2. D4/4 side: the centered 2x2 glyph stamp no longer uses fixed maroon; its color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/17/code.py:25:      - the center 6x6 stamp is maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/17/code.py:56:    - The original fixed center overwrite with maroon is also invalid: the stamp color now\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/17/code.py:82:      single variant: outputs must differ from both the fixed-maroon lattice-transfer case\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/15/code.py:67:#      maroon stamp. The two clues support two distinct inferences.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/15/code.py:212:    Read a palette legend from the top strip and a contour glyph from the 6x6 body's border, then combine both to build the periodic lattice and centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/15/code.py:222:    - Tile a 16x16 canvas with the phase using the legend-selected colors, then place a 2x2 maroon tiling of the reconstructed glyph in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/1/code.py:20:#    - Fused task: the structure still reads its opening direction from geometry, but it no longer trusts the first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/1/code.py:57:#    - Every structure has exactly one minority tooth color and exactly one opening direction recoverable from the tooth\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/1/code.py:246:    - Read each structure's tooth color and opening direction from the comb geometry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/38/code.py:16:#      offset, and centered 6x6 maroon stamp. Only the glyph shape changed the background tile.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/38/code.py:49:#      lattice phase and the maroon stamp together, but by different formulas: modulo-3 for background, scaling for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/38/code.py:52:#    - Output still uses only black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/38/code.py:130:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a variable-sized periodic lattice whose phase and maroon stamp placement are both controlled by the glyph's input placement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/38/code.py:141:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 into a 6x6 stamp, recolor its true cells to maroon, and place that stamp at a position obtained by scaling the input bbox top-left into the legal output stamp-origin range.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/40/code.py:15:#   Originally that produced an orange/black lattice and a maroon center stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/40/code.py:26:#   \"center glyph pixels are maroon\" are both invalid now and must be replaced with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/40/code.py:43:#   Foreground colors exclude black, orange, and maroon, so the fused output cannot\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/11/code.py:588:    # Input reds are placed exactly slide cells away in the opening direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/2/code.py:512:    \"\"\"Build L-shaped arm waypoints for _path_crossing_all / _path_through.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/39/code.py:12:#      canvas, and the same 3x3 glyph is tiled 2x2 as a centered 6x6 maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/39/code.py:25:#      denser period-4 lattice behind the centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/39/code.py:49:#    - `center = np.tile(motif, (2, 2))` still holds, but now the centered maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/39/code.py:68:#      lattice and one centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/39/code.py:188:    Decode the enlarged 4x4 contour glyph into a period-4 orange/black lattice and stamp a 2x2 maroon copy of that glyph at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/39/code.py:198:    - Fill a black 16x16 canvas by repeating that period-4 tile, then tile the original 4x4 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 8x8 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/20/code.py:26:#     - output is still a 16x16 orange/black period-3 lattice with a centered 6x6 maroon overlay\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/20/code.py:53:#         - both the repeated lattice and the maroon center now expose orientation, so a rotated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/20/code.py:79:#     - the maroon center reinforces the rule by displaying a four-quadrant rotation cycle derived\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/20/code.py:82:#     - only black, orange, and maroon appear in the output, preserving the original palette discipline\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/20/code.py:84:#       the maroon overwrite is confined to the central 6x6 square\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/20/code.py:161:    Decode a rotated asymmetric 3x3 glyph into an oriented period-3 lattice, then place a rotating maroon stamp at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/20/code.py:171:    - In the centered 6x6 region, place four maroon copies of the observed motif arranged as a rotation cycle: 0 degrees, clockwise 90, 180, and counterclockwise 90.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/22/code.py:31:#   Old logic: search for an L-shaped color with count 3, derive a corner, then test many\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/15/code.py:23:#    - Here: a structure first reads its tooth color and its opening direction from geometry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/15/code.py:49:#      ray is only used to infer the opening direction and slot stack; color performs the match.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/15/code.py:220:    - Read each structure's tooth color and opening direction from its geometry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/1/code.py:511:    \"\"\"Build L-shaped arm waypoints for _path_crossing_all / _path_through.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/1/code.py:10:#    In this combo, the output core is a non-rectangular connected shape (mostly L-shapes, plus\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/1/code.py:19:#    Small example: for a top+left target on an L-shape, the old logic would ask whether the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:25:#      a centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp of that glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:65:#    - The center overwrite assumes maroon can be painted on top of either lattice color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:79:#      black/orange periodic lattice everywhere, plus a maroon 2x2 stamp only in the centered\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:83:#      for the direct glyph-derived phase cells, and maroon for the center stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:167:    Reinterpret the colored 3x3 contour glyph as a directly copied phase mask, invert the lattice color roles, and stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/2/code.py:177:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 into the centered 6x6 region and recolor the glyph pixels to maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:19:#        2. tile the 3x3 glyph 2x2 into a 6x6 maroon center stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:22:#        2. the maroon glyph is moved to exactly one corner, chosen by glyph type\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:24:#        source: decode plus -> lattice -> 6x6 maroon plus-tiling at rows/cols 5..10\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:26:#                place one 3x3 maroon plus at the top-left corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:45:#    - The fused rule therefore uses a single 3x3 maroon glyph in one corner. This\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:58:#        2. exactly one corner contains the maroon glyph, and which corner it is varies\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:67:#        maroon overwrite only in one 3x3 corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:72:#    - The output uses only black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:149:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice with a black center void and a glyph-specific maroon corner stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:159:    - Overwrite the centered 6x6 area with pure black, then place one maroon 3x3 copy of the glyph into the corner assigned to that glyph class.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:162:    - The input contour now controls two output attributes at once: it still determines the orange lattice phase, and it also selects which corner receives the only maroon glyph while the center stays empty.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:224:    maroon_corners = [name for name, view in corner_views.items() if np.any(view == Color.MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/16/code.py:225:    if maroon_corners != [glyph_name]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/9/code.py:297:    - Recover every structure's opening direction and tooth-gap span from its solid back wall and spaced teeth.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D6/0/code.py:487:    \"\"\"Build L-shaped arm waypoints for _path_crossing_all / _path_through.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/9/code.py:24:#     - output stays a 16x16 orange/black period-3 lattice with a centered 6x6 maroon overlay\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/9/code.py:83:#     - the output still uses only black, orange, and maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/9/code.py:150:    Treat the colored 3x3 asymmetric glyph as an oriented phase code, then render a mirrored maroon stamp at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/9/code.py:161:    - In the centered 6x6 region, place four transformed maroon copies of the glyph: original, horizontal flip, vertical flip, and 180-degree rotation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:24:#     - output stays a 16x16 black/orange period-3 lattice with a centered 6x6 maroon stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:38:#       4. tile the rotated phase across 16x16, then stamp the observed 111/100/100 motif in maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:58:#     - the centered 6x6 maroon stamp is unchanged and safely overwrites the tiled lattice last\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:60:#     - a human sees the oriented glyph twice: once in the input and again as the 2x2 maroon stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:66:#     - only three colors appear in the output: black, orange, maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/10/code.py:167:    - Repeat the rotated phase tile over the 16x16 black canvas, then tile the observed motif 2x2 and recolor its true cells to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/29/code.py:35:#      maroon and still mean \"go left 4\"; therefore the solver must decode motion from shape only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/19/code.py:211:    - For every structure, read its opening direction from the tooth geometry and read its target color from the wall color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D14/0/code.py:513:    \"\"\"Build L-shaped arm waypoints for _path_crossing_all / _path_through.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:22:#    repeat one orange/black lattice -> stamp that glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:31:#    the earlier one on shared cells. The center stamp stays a single 2x2 maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:59:#    The output still uses only black, two layer colors, and one centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:178:    Decode two colored copies of the same contour glyph into shifted lattice layers, then place the shared glyph as a centered maroon seal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/21/code.py:188:    - Composite the two shifted lattices so the later bbox in row-major order overwrites the earlier one on overlap, then stamp the shared glyph tiled 2x2 in maroon inside the centered 6x6 window.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/15/code.py:24:#    whole column and returned the dense rectangle. Here the source core is an L-shape: think\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/15/code.py:27:#    silhouette of that L-shape rather than spanning an entire row/column. Example: if the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/15/code.py:32:#    L-shaped core canvas -> erase the dominant non-background fill color to 0. The result is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/15/code.py:35:#    The generator deliberately stays with one irregular family: a single corner-notch L-shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:17:#   output still consists of a tiled orange/black phase lattice plus a centered 2x2 maroon stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:51:#   comfortably larger than the fixed 6x6 maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:57:# - Foreground color is chosen from the same safe set excluding black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:69:#   maroon stamp. No extra markers are added.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:75:#   color, while the output still uses only black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/19/code.py:139:    - Tile the phase tile across that canvas, then place a centered 6x6 maroon stamp made by 2x2 tiling of the original glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/25/code.py:50:#       - Suppose the frame contains three slots: a unit cell, a domino, and an L-shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D15/1/code.py:80:#   - main() assumes marker components are color-5 L-shapes of area 3. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:26:#   - a maroon stamp is always the 2x2 tiling of the 3x3 glyph, so each stamp is 6x6\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:36:#     - output gets one centered 6x6 maroon stamp at (5, 5)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:62:#   - maroon stamps are large and repeated, making the regular spacing easy to see\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:156:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice and stamp a shifted 2x2 maroon stamp array.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:166:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 to form a 6x6 maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/4/code.py:170:    - The glyph carries two independent visible signals: its shape still determines the orange phase lattice, while its input position now controls the global offset of an evenly spaced four-stamp maroon array.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/13/code.py:323:    - Ray-cast outward from each structure's interior socket cells and collect the red components visible on each opening direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/5/code.py:148:    Decode the 3x3 contour cue into the original 16x16 periodic lattice, then stamp a mixed-symmetry 2x2 arrangement of that glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/5/code.py:158:    - In the centered 6x6 window, place four 3x3 maroon copies of the glyph using a mixed D4 layout:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/8/code.py:26:#    - D3/1 breaks the old color-shape binding: a plus may be orange, teal, maroon, etc.,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/8/code.py:31:#        glyphs in reading order = cross(teal), plus(maroon), diamond(teal), plus(orange)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D9/0/code.py:24:#    - Old logic: three L-shaped sprites outside = red, red, blue ->\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D9/0/code.py:25:#      every L-shaped hole becomes solid red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D9/0/code.py:26:#    - New logic: three L-shaped sprites outside = pattern A, pattern A,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D9/0/code.py:27:#      pattern B -> every L-shaped hole receives the aligned copy of pattern A.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/22/code.py:21:#    candidate slots, each with the same opening direction but its own exact\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/22/code.py:55:#    structure opening direction, so motion is axis-aligned and stays faithful to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/22/code.py:355:    - Parse each comb into individual per-tooth docking lanes inside the cavity, recovering both the opening direction and the exact rectangle shape for each lane.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:27:#   4. Put a centered 6x6 maroon stamp made from a plain 2x2 copy of the input glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:39:#   by one row, and the centered maroon stamp is built from mirrored copies of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:69:# - Inside the center, maroon is the only overlay color and stays confined to one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:184:    Decode one colored 3x3 contour glyph into a color-transferred phase lattice, then place a mirrored maroon stamp at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/28/code.py:195:    - Repeat the colored phase seed over the 16x16 black canvas, then place a centered 6x6 maroon mirror-collage\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/31/code.py:22:#   - 本融合版：例如某个 L 形槽位在框内右上角是红格；对应输入精灵先以另一朝向散落在外部，且红点落在其某个块的右上角。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/31/code.py:23:#     这个右上角不是目标位置，而是“旋转说明书”。solver 必须先解码为“旋转 180 度”，在块级把 L 形和标记格一起转正，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/34/code.py:34:#   the maroon center stamp and the orange/black lattice both rotate together.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/34/code.py:59:#   The output still uses the original three-color palette (black, orange, maroon), so the new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/34/code.py:175:    - Build the same 16x16 orange/black lattice and centered 2x2 maroon stamp as the canonical family would produce, then rotate the entire finished canvas by the recovered quarter-turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:18:#       color: any single color except black(0), grey(5), orange(7), maroon(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:23:#     stamp: the original 4x4 motif tiled 2x2 into a centered 8x8 maroon block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:24:#     colors_used: black(0), grey(5), orange(7), maroon(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:75:#    - The centered maroon stamp exposes the exact 4x4 motif geometry, giving the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:87:#      maroon for the stamp. The third lattice color always comes from the same logical\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:196:    Read a 4x4 contour code, expand it into a period-4 tricolor lattice, and stamp a centered maroon 2x2 copy of the motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/36/code.py:206:    - Repeat that 4x4 tricolor tile over a 16x16 canvas, then place a 2x2 maroon tiling of the original motif in the centered 8x8 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/37/code.py:31:    - each control is now a 3-cell L-shaped arrow touching exactly one border:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/37/code.py:64:    ctrl components, requires size-3 2x2 L-shapes, and decodes one launch site per\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/37/code.py:104:  - All ctrl cells belong to 1 or 2 size-3 L-shaped arrow components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/12/code.py:382:    - Parse each structure to recover its opening direction and the exact dock rectangle implied by the teeth.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:17:#      output is still 16x16 and still ends with a centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp of that glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:22:#      3. The maroon stamp is written last on top.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:38:#      stamps the 6x6 maroon H pattern. The center region therefore has two visible rhythms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:61:#    - Original final maroon overwrite remains valid and must still happen last.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:68:#    - The detail window is fixed to rows/cols 3..12 and the 6x6 maroon stamp sits at rows/cols\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:81:#      overlay, maroon stamp. The two tiled layers share the same orange/black palette and combine\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:90:#      maroon stamp copied from the input glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:226:    Decode one 3x3 contour glyph into a two-scale tiled scene whose background and center detail use different period tables, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/13/code.py:236:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon inside the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D5/1/code.py:26:#   complementary shape: its color is offset by how many maroon 9-rectangles the routed wire passes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D5/1/code.py:279:      color is increased by the number of maroon 9-rectangles that path passes through.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/24/code.py:12:# - Concrete behavior shift: if frame A contains an L-shaped hole and frame B a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:20:#      into a 6x6 maroon stamp -> place that stamp at the fixed centered box\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:24:#      3x3 into a 9x9 maroon stamp -> aim for the geometric center first, then snap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:30:#      snaps that to the nearest period-3 boundary, namely (3,3). The final maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:35:#      lattice decoding. This keeps the task readable while making the maroon region\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:62:#      the intended maroon-over-lattice overwrite already present in the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:67:#    - The maroon area becomes both larger and shifted relative to naive centering.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:75:#    - The output still has only three colors: black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:178:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a periodic 16x16 lattice, then overlay a larger maroon stamp snapped to the lattice grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:188:    - Tile the original glyph 3x3 to build a 9x9 stamp, recolor its True pixels to maroon, and place it at the nearest legal 3x3 tile boundary rather than at the old fixed center box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:191:    - The contour still determines the lattice phase, but the stamp geometry is now governed by two coupled constraints: it is larger because of 3x3 tiling, and it must sit on the lattice's own 3x3 boundary system, so the maroon region lands as a clean 3-by-3 block of tiles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:33:#      phase pattern of the decoded glyph. The centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:70:#      maroon center stamp still anchors the correspondence to the input glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:76:#      the maroon center stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:79:#      maroon keeps its center-stamp role, and the input's two non-orange colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:212:    Recover a 3x3 contour glyph from a textured 6x6 board, then render its decoded lattice with thicker black grid lines and the usual centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/22/code.py:222:    - Tile that 4x4 carrier across the 16x16 output and place a 2x2 maroon tiling of the recovered glyph in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/28/code.py:13:#    1-pixel L-shaped trail colored with that object's dominant fill color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/3/code.py:20:#      either L to fit either L-shaped hole. The fused logic is stricter: the two L pieces are only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:24:    - 原题从目标 3x3 块外的可通行格做普通 BFS，把所有可达 maroon 按步数远近搬回目标块。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:25:      例如某个 maroon 离入口 4 步、另一个 6 步，那么 4 步的先进入目标，即使那条路一直贴着墙走。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:26:    - 融合后仍然只允许沿 orange/maroon 的 4 连通路径到达，但“距离”不再是步数，而是：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:28:    - 具体小例子：一枚 maroon 在入口旁边的 2 格死胡同里，路径两格都被三面墙夹住，总代价可能是\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:29:      3 + 3 = 6；另一枚更远的 maroon 在较宽主通道深处，沿路 5 格每格只贴 1 面墙，总代价只有 5。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:44:    - 原 main() 依赖“可达 maroon 数 = 要填入目标的数量”。这一点仍保留，所以生成器只放 k 个可达\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:45:      maroon，其余 maroon 全都放在隔离口袋里做 distractor。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:47:    - 目标块固定在 11x11 的中心 3x3；除目标块外，其余单元只会是 floor、wall 或 maroon。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:51:    - 人类可以直接看到：有些 maroon 虽然步数更近，但卡在三面贴墙的死胡同；另一些更远，却位于\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:53:    - 由于目标块仍按 row-major 填入，观察者只需比较“哪些 maroon 消失了”，就能对照迷宫几何推断\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:56:    - 场景仍只有五种颜色，且各自语义稳定：orange 地板、magenta 墙、green/red 目标、maroon token。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:423:    Move the reachable maroon pixels with the smallest wall-contact path cost into the centered 3x3 target block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:427:    - Orange cells are walkable floor, magenta cells are maze walls, and maroon cells sit on floor cells inside the maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:430:    - Start from every floor/maroon cell directly adjacent to the destination block and traverse only floor or maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:432:    - Keep only reachable maroon pixels, rank them by this accumulated wall-neighbor cost, and place the closest ones into the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:433:    - Any maroon that moves is erased from its source cell and replaced by orange floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:435:    Key insight: In the maze, the winning maroons are not always the fewest steps away; wider passages can beat shorter but tighter dead ends because distance is driven by repeated contact with nearby walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:454:    maroons = [(int(expo[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:455:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:456:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:459:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/49/code.py:460:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/34/code.py:15:#    - The source core is now a non-rectangular L-shape: a filled rectangle with the corner opposite the control\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/34/code.py:28:#    - I use one non-rectangular family (L-shape) rather than mixing many silhouettes. That keeps the puzzle readable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/34/code.py:47:#    - The center object visibly has an L-shaped dense region, not a plain rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/34/code.py:48:#    - Outputs are sparse rather than dense, and their occupied colored cells still spread across the L-shape, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/11/code.py:38:      - 假设某个 slot 是 3 格 L 形，k=3\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/5/code.py:9:#    - Each corridor color receives a same-color 2x2 L-shaped legend glyph:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:15:#      sorts reachable maroons by flood-fill distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:19:#    - Sorting is intentionally decoupled from that path wave: once maroons are known to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:28:#      maroons; otherwise \"sorting\" would be invisible because every reachable token would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:38:#    - Erasing moved maroons back to floor=7 remains valid because the spec keeps the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:41:#    - Walls, destination, source maroons, and sealed distractor pockets are placed on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:47:#    - The output retains some outside maroons because only nine move; this exposes which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:126:def _reachable_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:129:    maroons: list[tuple[int, int, int]] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:132:            maroons.append((_euclid2(int(r), int(c), cr, cc), int(r), int(c)))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:133:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:134:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:152:    Pull the Euclidean-closest reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:155:    - Orange floor holds scattered maroon tokens, magenta wall cells, and one fixed 3x3 target block whose center is the unique red pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:159:    - Start from every floor/maroon cell that touches the target block in 8-neighbor sense, then flood-fill through floor+maroon with 8-connectivity; this is the reachability test and its path metric is Chebyshev-style 8-step BFS.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:160:    - Keep only maroon pixels reached by that wave, but rank them by Euclidean distance to the red center rather than by flood-fill distance; ties break by row then column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:161:    - Move the best k=min(9, reachable_count) maroons into the destination block in row-major order and erase those source cells back to orange floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/52/code.py:177:    ranked = _reachable_maroons(grid, dist8, cr, cc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D16/2/code.py:36:#       stage_2: \"fill every L-shaped hole with yellow, not red\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D9/3/code.py:36:#       avoids covering crossings or maroon junction rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/7/code.py:53:      suppose a slot is an L-shape:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:9:#      scattered maroon tokens outside the block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:11:#      ranked reachable maroons by increasing BFS distance, and wrote them into\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:14:#      1. Candidate maroons are ranked from far to near.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:26:#      added. With identical maroon tokens, D3 only changes the output when more\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:42:#    - The old `k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))` also breaks because the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:45:#      set should be erased; the extra near maroons must survive in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:50:#    - Source and distractor maroons are sampled only from floor cells outside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:57:#      effects co-occur: far maroons disappear while near ones remain, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:70:#      maroon moves, floor is restored, green stays as empty target cells, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:199:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:200:    maroons = [triple for triple in maroons if triple[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:201:    return dest_cells, fill_order, center, floor, maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:206:    Move the farthest reachable maroon pixels into the destination block while leaving the red center untouched.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:209:    - The board is an orange floor with optional magenta wall barriers and scattered maroon source pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:213:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells touching the target, walking only through floor or maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:214:    - Reachable maroon pixels are ranked from farthest to nearest by BFS distance, with row/column tie-breaks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:215:    - The chosen maroons are erased from their source positions and copied into the target in reverse row-major order starting from the lower-right, but the red center cell is always skipped.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:223:    dest_cells, fill_order, _center, floor, maroons = _analyze_grid(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:225:    maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:226:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:227:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:444:    dest_cells, fill_order, center, floor, maroons = _analyze_grid(inp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:445:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:446:    ordered_far = sorted(maroons, key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:447:    ordered_near = sorted(maroons)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/29/code.py:471:        \"reachable_count\": len(maroons),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D3/0/code.py:14:#       red L-shape x5, green L-shape x1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/15/code.py:92:#    - Turns keep the original L-shape vocabulary, so the scene stays readable:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:7:#   A canonical corridor sits beside the 3x3 destination block. The first maroon is within\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:9:#   them, and the fourth remains at distance 4 even after earlier maroons disappear. This\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:15:#   In the base task maroon cells were globally passable, so deleting one could not shorten any\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:16:#   route. Here only orange floor is traversable; a maroon may be used only as the final target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:23:#   Walls isolate one narrow chamber, so a human can see the front maroon disappear first,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:24:#   then notice that deeper maroons become newly available one by one. The untouched fourth\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:25:#   maroon demonstrates the path-length threshold.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:28:#   1. at least one maroon is collected by the fused solver,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:29:#   2. at least two collected maroons were not initially eligible under the threshold,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:30:#   3. an iterative solver without the threshold would collect strictly more maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:289:    Pull maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center, one shortest-path step at a time.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:297:    - Repeatedly recompute which maroon pixel is reachable from the destination through orange floor cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:298:    - A maroon qualifies only if its current shortest path length is at most 3, where the last step may enter the maroon but other maroons are not traversable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:299:    - On each iteration, move only the single nearest qualifying maroon into the next destination cell in row-major order, erase its source to floor, then recompute from the updated grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:300:    - Stop when the block is full or no maroon remains within the path-length limit.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:303:    - Removing one maroon can open a shorter route to deeper maroons, so the reachable set is dynamic; however the 3-step cap still prevents some connected maroons from ever being collected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/19/code.py:42:#    cyan/maroon pixels. Across examples, that local divider cue flips whether the first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D12/0/code.py:24:#    means pink, pink, orange; a teal source means teal, teal, maroon; a green source\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D12/0/code.py:71:    8: 9,  # teal -> maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/0/code.py:43:#    - 仍保留大部分 8 号竖线和少量 5 号普通直穿标记；9 号块只替换少数关键交叉，不让整张图变成大块 maroon 噪声。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/0/code.py:282:    Route endpoint tokens through pipe networks whose maroon rectangles act as quarter-turn mirrors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D3/1/code.py:41:#       - Suppose a hole has L-shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D3/1/code.py:42:#       - Outside sprites include L-shapes in red, red, yellow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D3/1/code.py:46:#       - The same L-shape hole now only has, for example, blue L-sprites outside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D3/1/code.py:47:#       - The new solver records \"L-shape -> blue\" directly and fills all matching\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/38/code.py:54:    - 真实竖直转弯和假陷阱入口都使用统一的 L 形几何, 视觉上容易并排比较.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/43/code.py:174:    - A magenta rectangular frame surrounds that block; some non-corner frame cells are replaced by maroon markers, and some frame cells are removed as 1-pixel openings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/43/code.py:178:    - A maroon frame marker is collectible only if the flood can touch it from the outside of the rectangle through one of the frame openings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D5/2/code.py:36:     legend piece, generation keeps a geometrically distinctive L-shaped anchor piece and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D5/2/code.py:411:LEGEND_THRESHOLD = {8: 4, 10: 5, 12: 9}        # min extent threshold per side for anchor L-shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D5/2/code.py:413:LEGEND_ARM_RANGE = range(1, 4)                 # arm width/height options for L-shape construction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D5/2/code.py:464:    \"\"\"Build an L-shaped anchor piece mask anchored at (0,0) of the side*side grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/35/code.py:32:    - 两个面积 5 的 slot 形状不同，左上的是真 L 形，右下的是横条。外部真实 piece 的摆放顺序被反过来，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/35/code.py:33:      因此按面积排序后，同面积 tie-break 会把“横条 piece”先贴到“L 形 slot”的位置。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:234:    - The background is the dominant color. Other cells form cyan wires, optional maroon rectangular junction blocks, and colored 3x3 tokens positioned two cells away from wire endpoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:15:#   In the original task, if six reachable maroon tokens are ranked closest first,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:18:#   so a cropped view of the old output would contain a maroon center once k >= 5.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:36:#   destination block and that at least one adjacent floor/maroon cell exists to seed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:41:#   Source maroons are sampled only from reachable floor cells outside the 3x3 block;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:47:#   maroons around it, making the \"skip center\" rule visible in 2-4 examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:49:#   The cropped output contains only green, red, and maroon inside one 3x3 block, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:94:def _rank_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:146:    ranked = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:155:    - The full 11x11 scene still contains orange floor, optional magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and one green 3x3 target block around a unique red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:159:    - Flood-fill from passable cells adjacent to the target through orange and maroon cells, ignoring magenta walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:160:    - Sort reachable maroon tokens by BFS distance, then by row and column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:164:    Key insight: The outside world is still needed to decide how many maroons qualify, but the returned grid is only the cropped destination state, with the center acting as a fixed reference point.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/25/code.py:167:    ranked = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D17/1/code.py:13:#   Original logic: if an L-shaped hole had outside L sprites in red/red/green, the solver counted colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/32/code.py:18:#      two L-shaped holes belong to the same D4 family but face different directions. In the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:18:#    - The original task does one static BFS, sorts every reachable maroon once, then fills the 3x3 target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:19:#    - This combo turns the wall into a local crumble mechanic: when a maroon is collected, every magenta wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:23:#         2. Take only the currently nearest reachable maroon layer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:29:#    - Only two dynamic gates are used, but each sample contains multiple layers and 5-8 collected maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:31:#    - The layout varies by optional filler maroons and grid rotation/flip, which keeps samples from looking cloned\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:36:#    - A collected maroon may alter the obstacle map, so the solver must mutate a working copy of the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:37:#    - The generator must keep trigger maroons near only their intended gates; otherwise 3x3 crumble would open\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:52:#    - The total collectible maroons stay within 9, so every moved maroon has a destination cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:53:#    - Trigger maroons are spaced so that their 3x3 crumble neighborhoods do not accidentally merge unrelated gates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:77:    \"\"\"Distance from the destination-adjacent frontier through floor/maroon cells; adjacent cells start at 1.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:107:    - final_work: grid after maroons are erased and dynamic walls have crumbled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:108:    - collected: maroons collected in layer order, row-major inside each layer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:165:def _static_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:166:    \"\"\"Reachable maroons under the original static-wall interpretation, used only for generator validation/metrics.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:168:    maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON) if (r, c) not in DEST_SET and dist[r, c] > 0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:169:    maroons.sort(key=lambda rc: (int(dist[rc[0], rc[1]]), rc[0], rc[1]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:170:    return maroons[:DEST_LIMIT]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:175:    Move maroons into the target block by repeatedly taking the current BFS-nearest layer and crumbling nearby walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:178:    - The grid is 11x11 with an orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and a fixed 3x3 green target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:180:    - Some maroons sit in rooms that are initially sealed by magenta barriers, while earlier reachable maroons sit next\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:184:    - Run BFS from floor/maroon cells adjacent to the target, but collect only the nearest reachable maroon layer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:185:    - After collecting that layer, erase those maroons to floor and turn every wall in each collected maroon's 3x3\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:187:    - Continue until no more maroons are reachable; place the collected maroons into the target block in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:252:    # Hall / room floors remain orange by default. Mark fixed and optional maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/26/code.py:279:    static_reachable = _static_reachable_maroons(inp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/14/code.py:66:- New combo-specific assumption: once the correct transform is chosen, the guide geometry is a clean L-shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/41/code.py:48:#      for each corridor color, a same-color 2x2 L-shape encodes the global turn\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/41/code.py:264:    - The bottom 2 rows are a legend band made of same-color 2x2 L-shapes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/2/code.py:309:    - Background cells surround orthogonal wire networks, optional maroon 9-rect pass-through blocks,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/45/code.py:16:#    - The original task sorted every reachable maroon token individually by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/45/code.py:27:#      distance 1: [(6,5,maroon)] -> output cell maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/45/code.py:29:#      The destination begins [grey, maroon, blue, ...] in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/45/code.py:34:#      maroon}. Each sample uses only 2-3 of them, so mixed layers are visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D2/3/code.py:356:LEGEND_THRESHOLD = {8: 4, 10: 5, 12: 9}       # min extent threshold per side for legend L-shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D2/3/code.py:358:LEGEND_ARM_RANGE = range(1, 4)                 # arm width/height options for L-shape construction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D2/3/code.py:404:    \"\"\"Build an L-shaped legend piece mask anchored at (0,0) of the side*side grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D12/1/code.py:28:#      old rule: L-shaped hole + outside L sprites in red/red/green -> fill red by plurality.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D12/1/code.py:29:#      new rule: L-shaped hole + outside L sprites all red -> fill red directly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:33:#    - 原来的 `maroons.sort()` 默认是 `(flood_distance,row,col)`; 融合后必须改成\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:36:#    - 原 solver 里“k = min(9, reachable_maroon_count)”仍成立; 新 generator 明确围绕这个容量上限造样例。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:145:def _reachable_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:151:    maroons = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:155:            maroons.append((rr, cc))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:156:    return maroons, dist\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:181:    maroons, dist = _reachable_maroons(grid, center)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:183:        source_order = _sort_sources_combo(maroons, center)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:185:        source_order = _sort_sources_legacy(maroons, dist)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:212:    maroons, dist = _reachable_maroons(grid, center)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:213:    combo_sources = _sort_sources_combo(maroons, center)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:214:    legacy_sources = _sort_sources_legacy(maroons, dist)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:215:    k = min(9, len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:226:        \"reachable\": len(maroons),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:236:    Pull reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:240:    - The board is an 11x11 orange floor with optional magenta walls and scattered maroon tokens.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:244:    - First flood-fill outward from floor cells touching the target block, moving only through floor or maroon cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:245:      and keep only maroon tokens that are reachable through that passable region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:246:    - Sort the reachable maroon tokens by Euclidean distance to the red center, nearest first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/47/code.py:252:    - Walls still matter, because they decide which maroon tokens are even eligible, but once eligibility is fixed,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/0/code.py:15:#      wires are still 8/5 networks, and maroon 9-regions are still embedded rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/0/code.py:16:#    - The new observable effect is on the transmitted far-end token only. A maroon rectangle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/0/code.py:47:#    - The rule is visible without using hidden ids: channels that cross a maroon rectangle produce\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/0/code.py:48:#      the same rest-shape on both ends; channels that avoid maroon keep the original complementary\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/0/code.py:265:    Transmit colored tokens through wire networks while maroon rectangles invert the outbound motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/0/code.py:278:      the parity of encountered maroon rectangles controls whether the transmitted complement flips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:29:      - colors stay orange floor(7), magenta frame/wall(6), green destination ring(3), red center(2), maroon tokens(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:30:      - movement is still based on 4-connected flood-fill through floor/maroon cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:31:      - each destination block still fills in row-major order with the closest assigned maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:34:      - maroons are assigned many:many: each token is claimed by the nearest reachable container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:49:      - each container gets at least one selected maroon from a region that is strictly nearer to that container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:50:      - at least one selected maroon comes from an overlap region reachable from both containers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:51:      - optional distractor maroons may appear inside the detached frame, unreachable from both containers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:57:      - globally rank reachable maroons and pour them into one container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:61:      - for each maroon, compare both distance maps and assign the token to the nearer block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:62:      - each block independently sorts its own assigned maroons and fills its own cells in row-major order\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:64:      - with centers at (1,1) and (9,9), a maroon near the upper-left corridor belongs only to the first block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:65:      - a maroon near the lower-right corridor belongs only to the second block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:66:      - a maroon near the middle lanes around the detached frame can be reached from both, so ownership must be decided before filling\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:84:    - original global `maroons[:k]` selection is invalid because each container has its own quota and ownership list\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:91:      - source maroons are sampled only from floor cells outside blocks and outside the frame boundary\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:99:      - every accepted sample has maroons owned by both containers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:100:      - every accepted sample includes at least one overlap maroon reachable from both containers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:108:    - forcing one private maroon per container plus one contested maroon keeps the rule readable from a few examples\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:223:    overlap_maroons = 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:224:    strict_owner_maroons = [0 for _ in containers]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:233:            overlap_maroons += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:238:                strict_owner_maroons[owner] += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:249:        \"overlap_maroons\": overlap_maroons,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:250:        \"strict0\": strict_owner_maroons[0] if strict_owner_maroons else 0,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:251:        \"strict1\": strict_owner_maroons[1] if len(strict_owner_maroons) > 1 else 0,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:258:    Pull maroon pixels into two separated 3x3 containers, each centered on a red marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:261:    - The background is orange floor with scattered maroon source pixels and a detached magenta frame in the middle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:265:    - For each destination block, run a flood-fill distance search through floor/maroon cells, with magenta cells acting as blockers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:266:    - Each reachable maroon is assigned to the nearest block; equal distances are broken by the row-major order of the red centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:267:    - Within each block, its assigned maroons are sorted by distance then row-major position, erased from their source cells, and written into that block in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:271:    - You must combine two BFS maps with an ownership step: first decide which block owns each maroon, then fill the two containers independently.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:290:    owned_maroons = [[] for _ in containers]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:296:        owned_maroons[owner].append((int(dists[owner][r, c]), r, c))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:299:        owned_maroons[idx].sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:300:        chosen = owned_maroons[idx][: len(dest_cells)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/31/code.py:446:    if features[\"overlap_maroons\"] < 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/1/code.py:14:#    wire endpoints, teal/grey wires route colors across the grid, and maroon rectangles remain\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/1/code.py:15:#    embedded inside those wires. The change is only the role of the maroon rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/1/code.py:24:#    If its route contains a 2x3 maroon rectangle (area 6), the bottom endpoint still receives\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/1/code.py:25:#    an X. If the route instead contains a 3x3 maroon rectangle (area 9), the bottom endpoint\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/1/code.py:48:#    inspect maroon rectangles and compare examples where a 2x2 / 2x3 rectangle still lets the far\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/1/code.py:253:    Route endpoint tokens across the wire network while maroon rectangles act as parity gates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D8/1/code.py:268:    - The maroon rectangle is no longer just a connector. Its width-by-height parity is the gate,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:20:# - D13/0 is enforced by generation: the number of reachable maroon sources is exactly k, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:28:#   distractor maroons remain to preserve the original flood-fill reachability cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:55:def _reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dest_cells: list[tuple[int, int]], dest_set: set[tuple[int, int]], floor: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:82:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9) if int(dist[r, c]) < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:83:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:84:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:93:    Move every reachable maroon source into the row-major prefix of a marked 3x3 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:96:    - bg = orange floor, optional magenta walls, scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:101:    - Flood-fill from cells adjacent to the destination through floor/maroon cells to find reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:102:      maroon sources.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:105:    - Erase the collected source maroons back to floor. On valid instances, the reachable maroon count\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:108:    Key insight: The red pixel no longer just locates the block; it encodes how many reachable maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:109:    should be collected. Walls still matter because only flood-fill-reachable maroons participate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/27/code.py:117:    reachable = _reachable_maroons(grid, dest_cells, dest_set, floor)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/20/code.py:22:    if two L-shaped holes appear inside the same frame, one ringed by color 2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:18:#    - Change 1 (D5/1): source tokens can use several visible colors instead of only maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:21:#      blue -> yellow -> teal -> maroon, and within each color group they are sorted by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:25:#      [(d=0, blue), (d=1, maroon), (d=2, yellow), (d=3, blue)].\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:26:#      Original task / D5-only variant would place colors [blue, maroon, yellow, blue].\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:27:#      This combo places [blue, blue, yellow, maroon] because both blue tokens must be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:28:#      consumed before any yellow, and yellow before maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:30:#    - Restrict token colors to a compact palette {blue=1, yellow=4, teal=8, maroon=9}.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:40:#    - `maroons.sort()` was enough before. Now the key must be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/8/code.py:196:    - Collect every reachable token, sort them first by the fixed visible color-group order blue -> yellow -> teal -> maroon, then within each color by flood-fill distance and row/column, and place the chosen colors into the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:17:#   Original task: reachable maroon pixels were moved into the 3x3 target block, so the chosen\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:18:#   source cells turned back into orange floor; unreachable maroons stayed where they were.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:19:#   This combo changes both ends at once: chosen reachable maroons are copied into the target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:20:#   block but remain maroon at their original positions, while unreachable maroons are erased.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:21:#   Example sketch: if two reachable maroons and one walled-off maroon are present, the original\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:22:#   output would keep only two maroons inside the block plus the unreachable distractor; the new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:23:#   output keeps the two reachable maroons in place, adds two maroons inside the block, and removes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:27:#   maroons stay in place and the destination uses a single color. To avoid hidden/unobservable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:28:#   degrees of freedom, the generator only creates 2..9 reachable maroons, so every reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:29:#   maroon is copied and none are silently excluded by the ranking step. It also forces at least\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:33:#   walls=6, floor=7, maroons=9. It also assumes one red center, a 3x3 target around it, at least\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:34:#   one passable opening adjacent to the block, and maroons placed only on floor cells outside the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:37:#   Walls are painted only outside the destination block; maroons are sampled only from floor cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:40:#   copies, reachable corridors keep their maroons, and blocked regions become clean floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:42:#   Across a few examples, a solver can see a stable contrast: maroons connected to a corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:43:#   opening appear twice in the output, while maroons behind walls disappear. No hidden color-value\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:98:def _reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[list[tuple[int, int, int]], np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:126:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:127:    reachable = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:134:    Copy reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center, while erasing blocked ones.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:137:    - Orange floor carries scattered maroon pixels, and magenta walls may carve the floor into connected and sealed-off regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:141:    - Flood-fill outward from floor or maroon cells touching the destination block, traversing only orange floor and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:143:    - Those reachable sources stay maroon in place, but any maroon pixel not reached by the flood-fill is erased to orange floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:146:    - The output separates maroons by connectivity, not by raw proximity: corridor-connected maroons survive and also appear inside the block, while wall-isolated maroons disappear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:158:    reachable, _dist = _reachable_maroons(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:160:    all_maroons = {(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/24/code.py:161:    unreachable = all_maroons - reachable_set\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/0/code.py:18:#    - 删除原题输入里的青色管道和灰色 crossing 标记；中部改成若干条横向 maroon(9) 墙带，每条墙带只留一个小缺口。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D14/2/code.py:11:#    Variant: the seed is an L-shaped yellow border component in one corner, e.g.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:8:#    - 原题会把 `floor+maroon` 都当作 BFS 通道，所以一条走廊里的整串栗色会一次性全部变成候选，再按距离从近到远选前 k 个。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:18:#    - 原先把 maroon 自己的 BFS 距离直接读出 `dist[r,c]` 不再成立，因为 maroon 不在 BFS 图里；现在距离改为“相邻已达地板的最短距离 + 1”，并额外兼容直接贴住目标块的栗色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:34:#    - main() 依赖“被收集的栗色底下应当是 floor”；generator 通过先雕 floor 再覆盖 maroon 来保证这一点。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:138:def _reachable_frontier_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:168:    maroons = [(d, r, c) for (r, c), d in best.items()]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:169:    maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:170:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:182:    initial_frontier = _reachable_frontier_maroons(work, dest_cells, dest_set, floor)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:185:        frontier = _reachable_frontier_maroons(work, dest_cells, dest_set, floor)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:229:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:230:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:231:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:233:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:234:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:244:    Iteratively move the farthest currently exposed maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the lone red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:247:    - Orange cells are the only traversable background; green/red destination cells, magenta walls, and maroon source pixels all behave as solid obstacles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:248:    - A unique red cell marks the middle of a green 3x3 destination block, while maroon pixels sit on narrow floor corridors or in isolated pockets outside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:252:    - At each step, any maroon touching the reached floor region is collectible; choose the farthest such maroon (ties: row, then column), erase it back to floor, and recompute reachability.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:253:    - Stop when the 3x3 block has taken 9 maroons or when no maroon is currently reachable, then write the collected maroons into the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:256:    - Because maroon pixels now block the flood-fill instead of extending it, a removed maroon can reveal new maroons behind it; the final survivors therefore depend on both the iterative unlocking process and the reversed distance preference.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/22/code.py:55:  - Region pieces span their whole partition bbox via sparse L-shaped pieces,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/1/code.py:260:    - The background is the most common color. Non-background cells form cyan pipe networks, optional maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/6/code.py:10:- 原题的控制源是边缘单像素；这里改成 3 像素、4 连通、单色的 L 形箭头。箭头朝向即发射方向：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/6/code.py:21:- 与原题相比，解题链从“看边缘单点”变成“先识别 L 形箭头朝向，再读箭头颜色的动作语义”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/6/code.py:59:- 所有控制像素恰好组成 1 或 2 个 3 像素、单色、4 连通的 L 形箭头；generator 保证这一点。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/6/code.py:367:    - 先把边缘控制对象识别成 3 像素 L 形箭头，并由形状恢复 inward ray 的方向与 split 行/列。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:20:#    (4..6,7), (7,4..6), a maroon at (2,2) is unreachable in the original rule because\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:36:#    - Sorting only matters if more than 9 reachable maroons exist; the generator now\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:37:#      always places exactly 10 reachable maroons and rejects samples where Chebyshev and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:45:#    diagonally positioned maroons, which directly exposes the 8-connectivity change.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:46:#    Because only 9 of 10 maroons move, the leftover source position reveals the distance\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:50:#    wall ring, diagonal openings, and maroon pool stay visually separate, so the input\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:56:#    diagonal corner cells to remain floor or maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:139:def _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, dist):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:141:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:142:    maroons = [triple for triple in maroons if triple[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:143:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:144:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:167:    ranked = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, dist)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:181:    Pull the reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block centered on the unique red cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:185:    - Magenta walls can seal the destination orthogonally while maroon source pixels sit on floor cells outside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:188:    - Start from every passable cell that touches the destination in the 8-neighborhood, then flood-fill through floor/maroon cells using 8-connectivity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:189:    - Rank reachable maroon pixels by the resulting 8-direction shortest-path distance (Chebyshev-style), breaking ties by row then column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:190:    - Move the closest ranked maroons into the destination in row-major order and erase their original positions back to floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:203:    return _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, dist)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/1/code.py:209:    return _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, dist)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/9/code.py:34:#    - Small trace: consider two L-shaped slots that are the same under rotation but face\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D4/1/code.py:389:LEGEND_THRESHOLD = {8: 4, 10: 5, 12: 9}       # min extent threshold per side for legend L-shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D4/1/code.py:391:LEGEND_ARM_RANGE = range(1, 4)                 # arm width/height options for L-shape construction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D4/1/code.py:437:    \"\"\"Build an L-shaped legend piece mask anchored at (0,0) of the side*side grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:14:#    The original task already moves reachable maroon tokens into the 3x3 destination by BFS distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:19:#    but do not reach the outside ring where most source maroons live.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:35:#    Humans can compare 2-4 examples and spot the rule because the only moving parts are maroon tokens and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:47:#    - At least one full tunnel reaches the exterior, so reachable maroons can always be placed outside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:48:#    - Distractor pockets are sealed by construction, so unreachable maroons remain unreachable even after\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:120:def _sorted_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dist: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:121:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:122:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:123:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:124:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:129:    Pull the reachable maroon tokens through the true frame openings into the 3x3 target block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:138:    - Start a flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination block and move through orange or maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:139:    - Only maroon tokens in the same 4-connected component as a real doorway sequence are candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:140:    - Sort reachable maroons by BFS distance, then by row and column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:141:    - Replace the chosen source cells with orange floor and write the chosen maroons into the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:145:      near the green block is not enough; the path must cross both frames to access the outside maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:158:    maroons = _sorted_reachable_maroons(grid, dist)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:160:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:161:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:272:    maroons = _sorted_reachable_maroons(inp, dist)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:273:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/3/code.py:274:    for _, r, c in maroons[:k]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D4/3/code.py:406:LEGEND_THRESHOLD = {8: 4, 10: 5, 12: 9}      # min extent threshold per side for legend L-shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D4/3/code.py:408:LEGEND_ARM_RANGE = range(1, 4)                # arm width/height options for L-shape construction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/21/code.py:44:  - Suppose k=2 and a 3-cell L-shaped slot is surrounded by teal walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:15:#   decision in the output. Example: if three maroon tokens can be reached from the 3x3 target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:16:#   block and two are trapped behind magenta walls, then the output shows three maroons inside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:22:#   Every generated example contains all three cues simultaneously: destination maroons,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:27:#   maroon=9, trace=5, unreachable=1. The solver still only reads original input colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:29:#   maroons only on floor cells outside that block, and adds a separate sealed 4x4 wall pocket in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:30:#   one corner so at least one unreachable maroon can always be placed without overlap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:36:#   capacity, so every reachable maroon is one of the collected tokens. That avoids leftover\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:37:#   reachable maroons outside the block and keeps the output limited to the intended three cues.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:92:    assert q, \"there must be at least one floor or maroon cell adjacent to the destination block\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:106:    Classify maroon tokens by reachability, move the reachable ones into the center block, and leave visible evidence behind.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:110:    - Green cells form the rest of that destination block, magenta cells act as walls, and maroon cells are scattered tokens on the floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:113:    - Flood-fill outward from floor-or-maroon cells touching the destination block, stopping at magenta walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:114:    - Sort reachable maroon cells by BFS distance, then by row and column; place them into the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:115:    - Each reachable maroon leaves a gray trace at its source position, while each unreachable maroon is recolored blue and stays in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:118:    - The output reveals the full connectivity judgment: maroon inside the block shows which tokens were chosen, gray shows which outside tokens were reachable, and blue shows which ones walls cut off.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:131:    maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:132:    reachable = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in maroons if int(dist[r, c]) < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/11/code.py:133:    unreachable = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in maroons if int(dist[r, c]) >= 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D3/1/code.py:291:    - Background cells surround a connected cyan/grey/maroon wire network plus 3x3\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D15/0/code.py:19:#   The multicolor legend piece is still an L-shape. Its top arm and left arm now have intentionally different\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D15/0/code.py:316:    - The legend sprite is still L-shaped, but now its top arm and left arm have different lengths, which acts as a direction cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D15/0/code.py:324:    - The legend now provides two signals at once: its internal 2x2 colors still define the piece recoloring, while its outer L-shape asymmetry determines the global post-assembly rotation direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D15/0/code.py:421:    \"\"\"Build an L-shaped legend piece whose longer arm encodes the final rotation direction.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/37/code.py:16:#    - Replace the original \"many scattered maroons -> one center block\" layout with one shared\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D4/3/code.py:43:#     - New task: place a red L-shaped tetromino; solver extracts that component,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D11/0/code.py:31:#      original: two L-shaped red sprites + one L-shaped green sprite outside ->\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D11/0/code.py:32:#      an L-shaped hole is filled red by plurality.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D11/0/code.py:33:#      variant: one L-shaped green sprite outside -> the L-shaped hole is filled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D3/3/code.py:17:#   from red near the source, through grey then maroon, back to red near the arrival end.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/4/code.py:30:    - Example holes after sorting: [area 4 L-shape at left, area 4 bar at right,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/4/code.py:33:      scattered so the bar appears earlier in the input ordering than the L-shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:11:#     source_selection: unchanged flood-fill reachability through floor/maroon via 4-neighbors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:17:#       old: the red center could be overwritten if enough maroons were moved\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:34:#       moved: only the closest 8 maroons enter the outer ring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:35:#       preserved: the red center stays red and 2 farther reachable maroons remain outside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:37:#       the partial frontier bends around the perimeter, and saturated cases show a full maroon ring with a red hole\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:43:#       - 4..7 reachable maroons so the spiral prefix is visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:44:#       - 9..11 reachable maroons so skipping the center differs from the pure spiral variant that would fill it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:53:#       - output construction must preserve color 2 at (cr,cc) even when more than 8 reachable maroons exist\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:56:#       - dense-mode examples have at least 9 reachable maroons so the center-skip behavior is exercised\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:58:#     - source maroons are placed only on reachable floor cells, never in the destination or on walls\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:59:#     - extra reachable maroons in dense mode are chosen outside the first 8 ranked cells, so the solver deterministically leaves them behind\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:60:#     - distractor maroons are placed only on unreachable floor cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:169:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center, tracing a spiral that leaves the center untouched.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:172:    - Orange floor cells contain scattered maroon tokens, while magenta walls may block some corridors near the target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:176:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination through floor/maroon cells; only reachable maroons are movable candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:181:    - Two constraints interact: connectivity still decides which maroons qualify, but the destination now behaves like a spiral track wrapped around a permanent red hole.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:200:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:201:    maroons = [triple for triple in maroons if triple[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:202:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:204:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/7/code.py:205:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D12/0/code.py:16:#   grey crossing markers (5), optional maroon pass-through rectangles (9), and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:125:def _bfs_ranked_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, cr: int, cc: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:152:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON) if dist[r, c] >= 0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:153:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:154:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:163:    ranked = _bfs_ranked_maroons(out, cr, cc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:240:    Pull the closest straight-line visible maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:248:    - A ray crosses only orange floor and stops at its first non-floor cell; that cell is a candidate only if it is maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:252:    - Being in the same room is no longer enough. The magenta frame puts the block in a corner-biased viewing position, so many maroon pixels are flood-fill reachable but still ignored because no straight ray sees them first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:386:    total_maroons = int((inp == MAROON).sum())\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:387:    if total_maroons < TOTAL_MAROON_RANGE[0] or total_maroons > TOTAL_MAROON_RANGE[1]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:396:    bfs_ranked = _bfs_ranked_maroons(inp, cr, cc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:397:    bfs_only_maroons = {(r, c) for _, r, c in bfs_ranked} - visible_cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/42/code.py:398:    if not bfs_only_maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:31:#   - One maroon trigger sits in the first annulus and one in the second annulus. Collecting the first trigger\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:33:#     segment from the outer frame. Additional maroons wait outside the outer frame and are only collectible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:36:#   - Original task: run one static BFS, keep all reachable maroons, sort once, then fill the destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:42:#       5. Re-run BFS again. The outer-border maroons are now reachable and are collected layer by layer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:44:#       * more maroons move into the 3x3 block;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:52:#   - The first two annuli each contain exactly one trigger maroon. This prevents the dynamic process from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:59:#       * compute reachable maroons,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:66:#       * total collectible maroons never exceeds the 9 destination cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:72:#   - Unreachable distractors are placed in the opposite sealed corridors. They stay visibly maroon in the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:79:#       * later collected maroons line up beyond the newly opened gates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:398:    Pull maroon pixels into the 3x3 block, but only after they unlock nested wall gates layer by layer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:406:    - Run BFS from passable cells adjacent to the destination through floor and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:407:    - Collect only the nearest BFS layer of reachable maroons at a time. After the first-annulus layer is collected, a short middle-frame gate disappears; after the second-annulus layer is collected, a short outer-frame gate disappears.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:408:    - Recompute BFS after each wall change, continue layer by layer, erase every moved source to floor, and fill the destination cells in row-major order with the collected maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:410:    Key insight: Reachability is no longer static. The nested frames define a staged escape path, and the visible wall removals prove that later maroons are not initially reachable; they become collectible only because earlier BFS layers crack open the next shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:422:    maroons = [\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:427:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/53/code.py:428:    chosen = maroons[: len(DEST_CELLS)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/34/code.py:21:      L-shaped slots inside the frame and one green 1-cell slot elsewhere.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:29:#      orange floor, optional magenta walls, and scattered maroon source pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:30:#    - Reachability is unchanged: only maroons connected to the destination through floor/maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:36:#      smaller flood-fill distance, and if a row still contains several maroons at the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:38:#    - Example trace for reachable maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:46:#    - If reachable maroons are <= 9, all of them move and ranking becomes invisible. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:47:#      generator therefore uses 10-14 reachable sources so some maroons remain behind.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:55:#      non-maroon non-destination ring cell. The generator reserves one adjacent floor cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:56:#    - BFS through {floor, maroon} still defines eligibility. What changes is only ranking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:57:#    - The original `maroons.sort()` encoded (distance,row,col). In the combo, ranking must become\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:60:#    - Source maroons are sampled only from reachable floor cells outside the destination block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:68:#    - With >9 reachable maroons, the output exposes the rule through which maroons remain behind.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:69:#      In particular, some earlier-in-column maroons on the same row stay put because a nearer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:70:#      maroon later in that row is selected first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:75:#      maroons move versus remain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:78:#      rows containing multiple reachable maroons require a second observation: closer-in-corridor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:79:#      maroons win within that row, and equal-distance ties within the row read left-to-right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:94:#    - `_rank_key(..., \"fused\")` assumes distance values are defined for every candidate maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:209:    maroons = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:213:            maroons.append((int(r), int(c), d))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:214:    maroons.sort(key=lambda t: _rank_key(t[0], t[1], t[2], mode))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:216:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:217:    chosen = {(r, c) for r, c, _d in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:228:    Move reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 destination around the red center, using a row-first fused ranking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:231:    - The grid is always 11x11 with a fixed green 3x3 target around one red center, orange floor, optional magenta walls, and maroon pixels scattered on floor cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:232:    - Some maroons are flood-fill reachable from the target through floor/maroon corridors; others may be sealed off behind walls as distractors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:235:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells adjacent to the target, traversing only floor or maroon cells, and keep only reachable maroons as candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/35/code.py:237:    - Move up to nine ranked maroons into the destination in destination row-major order, and clear their source cells back to floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:23:#    - Original rule: a reachable maroon near one corridor gap is moved into the 3x3 target and its old\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:24:#      cell turns back into orange; an unreachable maroon behind a wall stays maroon; the whole 11x11 grid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:26:#    - Fused rule: that same reachable maroon still moves into the target, but its source cell becomes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:27:#      gray(5) to mark \"collected\". A blocked maroon in a sealed corner becomes blue(1) to mark \"rejected\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:31:#      maroon inside the target = packed token, gray = consumed reachable source, blue = unreachable source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:35:#      maroon tokens, gray traces, blue rejects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:48:#    - Gray traces are only meaningful for moved sources, so generator places exactly k reachable maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:53:#      coordinate sets. Corner pockets are isolated by added wall cells before maroons are placed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:57:#      rejects, and maroon packed tokens, but the layout is still structured: blue is forced into sealed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:58:#      crop corners, gray is forced onto reachable crop cells, and maroon fill stays inside the 3x3 target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:182:    Pack reachable maroon tokens into the central 3x3 target, leave gray pickup traces, repaint blocked maroons blue, then crop to the target neighborhood.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:186:    - Magenta wall segments create corridor gaps and sealed pockets around that target, while maroon tokens sit on floor cells outside the 3x3 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:189:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the target through orange/maroon cells, then rank reachable maroons by BFS distance with row-major tie-breaks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:190:    - Move the closest reachable maroons into the 3x3 target in row-major order, turn each consumed source gray, and recolor every unreachable maroon blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/32/code.py:194:    - The crop hides the distant corridors, so the important evidence is local: maroon inside the 3x3 block means \"selected\", gray means \"reachable and consumed\", and blue means \"blocked out by walls\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:48:#      a 3-cell L-shaped corner bite produces a 2-lane diagonal band.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D4/3/code.py:261:    Send split 3x3 tokens through the wire permutation, using an asymmetric pair of complementary L-shapes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:19:#      maroon cells, and anything beyond the 3x3 capacity simply stays outside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:24:#      If reachable maroons exceed that capacity, the spill does not stay put:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:25:#      the extra reachable maroons continue into the one-cell-thick outer ring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:29:#      If 13 reachable maroons exist, output fills the first 13 square cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:30:#      If 19 reachable maroons exist, output fills all 16 square cells and then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:33:#      extra maroons would remain at their source locations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:47:#    - \"overflow maroons are untouched\" is invalid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:56:#      never collide with walls and source/distractor maroons never start inside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:61:#    - Overflow is directly visible because the maroon fill expands from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:62:#      square into a second surrounding layer, not just \"some maroons remain\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:76:#      the square is full, the same maroon payload continues into the ring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:211:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into a variable-size square, then spill overflow into its surrounding ring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:214:    - Orange floor contains optional magenta walls and scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:218:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells touching the square, traversing only floor and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:219:    - Sort reachable maroon pixels by BFS distance, then by row and column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:220:    - Fill the square in row-major order first; if reachable maroons still remain, continue filling the one-cell-thick outer ring around that square in row-major order. Moved maroons are erased back to floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:240:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:241:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:242:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/17/code.py:244:    moved = maroons[: min(len(targets), len(maroons))]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/48/code.py:27:    - Example: suppose the frame contains five identical L-shaped holes arranged as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:11:#     connectivity: candidate maroons are still determined only by 4-connected flood-fill through floor/maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:14:#       old: sort reachable maroons by (bfs_distance, row, col)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:19:#       old: write the chosen maroons into the 3x3 block in row-major order\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:32:#       setup: 6 reachable maroons, all of them move\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:37:#       setup: 10 reachable maroons on the same bfs shell around the destination\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:38:#       original: 9 chosen maroons are the row-major earliest shell cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:39:#       combo: 9 chosen maroons are the clockwise-earliest shell cells from the top\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:40:#       visible_difference: the leftover outside maroon moves to a different side of the ring, even though the destination ends up full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:56:#       - walls remain hard blockers because bfs only walks on floor/maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:60:#       - generator can no longer assume \"exactly k reachable maroons\" is enough to expose every change\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:63:#       - angle-visible boards must guarantee a same-distance shell with at least 10 maroons and different row-vs-angle top-9 subsets\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:66:#     - source maroons are placed only on reachable floor cells, never inside the destination or on walls\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:67:#     - distractor maroons are placed only on unreachable floor cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:171:def _rank_reachable_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:178:    maroons = [\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:183:    maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (t[0], t[1], t[2], t[3]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:184:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:187:def _row_rank_reachable_maroons(dist: np.ndarray, maroons: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:188:    return sorted((int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in maroons)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:203:    reachable_maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere((grid == 9) & (dist < 10**9))]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:204:    moved = min(len(fill_order), len(reachable_maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:205:    angle_ranked = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, dist, cr, cc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:206:    row_ranked = _row_rank_reachable_maroons(dist, reachable_maroons)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:213:    angle_active = 1 if len(reachable_maroons) > len(fill_order) and angle_chosen != row_chosen else 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:216:        \"reachable\": len(reachable_maroons),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:224:    Move reachable maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center using clockwise tie-breaks and a spiral fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:227:    - Orange floor cells form the passable background, magenta walls may block parts of it, and maroon tokens sit on some floor cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:231:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination, treating floor and maroon as traversable; only reachable maroons are eligible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:232:    - Sort eligible maroons by BFS distance, then break same-distance ties by clockwise angle around the red center starting from straight up.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:233:    - Move the first nine-or-fewer maroons: erase their source cells back to floor and write them into the destination along a fixed clockwise outer-to-inner spiral.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:236:    - The same center controls both decisions: outside the block it orders tied maroons by rotation, and inside the block it lays the moved maroons down in the matching clockwise spiral.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:252:    maroons = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, dist, cr, cc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:253:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:254:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/15/code.py:480:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid =