)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:131:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:132:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:163:    Move the nine edge-nearest reachable maroon pixels into the centered 3x3 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:166:    - The board is 11x11 with orange floor, optional magenta wall barriers, scattered maroon pixels,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:173:      and maroon cells but never through magenta walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:174:    - Among the maroon pixels reached by that flood-fill, rank them by the minimum Manhattan distance\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:176:    - Move the first nine ranked maroons (or all of them if fewer exist) into the destination block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:181:    corridor length. A maroon that is geometrically close to one side of the block can outrank another\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:182:    maroon whose actual path from the center is shorter.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:194:    maroons = _reachable_maroons_sorted(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:195:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:196:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:330:    new_rank = {(r, c) for _, r, c in _reachable_maroons_sorted(probe)[:9]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:382:    reachable_maroons = _reachable_maroons_sorted(inp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:383:    if len(reachable_maroons) <= 9:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/38/code.py:397:    new_top9 = {(r, c) for _, r, c in reachable_maroons[:9]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:18:#       optional maroon 9-rect pass-through blocks inside the cyan/grey wire.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:401:      optional maroon pass-through rectangles, and 3x3 tokens near wire endpoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/0/code.py:15:#     solids: 2 basin colors still build bottom-anchored walls / L-shapes / short stair blocks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:14:#    - Original task ranked reachable maroons the same way as before, but then wrote them into all 9\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:20:#    - Example with k=6 reachable maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:35:#    - Generator never places walls or maroons inside the 3x3 destination block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:87:def _reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dest_cells: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:116:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:117:    maroons = [triple for triple in maroons if triple[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:118:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:119:    return maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:124:    Move the nearest reachable maroon pixels into the green frame around the unique red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:127:    - The board uses orange floor, optional magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and one red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:131:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the 3x3 destination block, traveling through orange or maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:132:    - Rank reachable maroon tokens by BFS distance, then by row and column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/40/code.py:152:    reachable = _reachable_maroons(grid, dest_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:17:     L-shaped arrow is attached near the tail side. The arrow is 8-connected to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:10:#       - reachable maroons are selected by BFS distance from the central 3x3 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:11:#       - maroons cut off by magenta walls are ignored and remain where they are.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:13:#       - D18/2 changes those blocked maroons into active movers that travel along the wall network.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:18:#     - Put blocked maroons in 1-cell side pockets between the two rings; each pocket touches the wall graph through two short connectors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:22:#       - a top-pocket maroon cannot be reached from the center because the top inner wall cell is closed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:25:#       - the same top-pocket maroon first attaches to adjacent magenta wall cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:27:#       - if that mouth is an inner opening on another side, the maroon becomes reachable and may join the central fill,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:30:#       - the new wall mouths are not cosmetic: they change both the nearest target of blocked maroons and the final ranking pool for the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:34:#     - The generator always includes both outcomes: one blocked maroon that reaches an inner opening and one that stops at an outer opening.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:37:#       - unreachable maroons can no longer be ignored before ranking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:38:#       - clearing only originally reachable sources is no longer sufficient because blocked maroons relocate first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:40:#       - blocked maroons must touch the wall graph; the generator guarantees this with side pockets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:42:#       - two blocked maroons should not compete for one target opening; the generator probes the layout and rejects collisions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:43:#       - pocket sides cannot have an inner opening on the same side, otherwise the pocket maroon would already be reachable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:46:#     - Reachable source maroons are sampled only from floor cells that are not pockets and not any potential opening cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:48:#     - The wall network is a clean square-with-frame motif, so widened mouths and moved maroons stand out immediately.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:302:def _move_blocked_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:315:    maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:316:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:317:    for r, c in maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:406:    staged, moved = _move_blocked_maroons(np.asarray(grid, dtype=int), CENTER_R, CENTER_C, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:408:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(staged == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:409:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:410:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:411:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[: min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:427:    Route blocked maroon pixels to the nearest wall mouth, then fill the center block with the closest reachable maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:431:    - Magenta walls form an inner ring and an outer frame, with visible side openings of width 1 or 2 and a few maroon pixels trapped in side pockets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:434:    - First, flood-fill reachability from the destination through floor and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:435:    - Any maroon that is still blocked travels along adjacent magenta wall cells to the nearest open wall mouth; inner mouths make it newly reachable, outer mouths only relocate it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:436:    - After those relocations, recompute reachability, rank reachable maroons by distance then row-major tie-break, and move the closest ones into the 3x3 destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:439:    - The wall openings matter twice: they are both pass-through corridors for the center flood-fill and the landing targets for previously unreachable maroons, so extra or wider mouths can change which maroons ultimately enter the block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:451:    staged, _ = _move_blocked_maroons(grid, cr, cc, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:454:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(staged == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:455:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:456:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:458:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:459:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:497:    staged_probe, moved_probe = _move_blocked_maroons(probe, CENTER_R, CENTER_C, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:42:#    - Walls are written only outside dest_set. Source and distractor maroons are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:49:#      still teaches \"reachable maroons only\" before the write-path twist.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:170:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the irregular destination shape using a spiral-with-skips fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:173:    - Orange floor cells may be split by magenta walls, and maroon tokens sit on some floor cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:177:    - Recover the full red+green container, then flood-fill outward through floor/maroon cells touching it to find reachable maroon candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:178:    - Rank reachable maroons by BFS distance, then by row and column, erase the closest ones from their source cells, and place them into the container.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:182:    - Two geometric inferences interact: walls still decide which maroons are eligible, but the destination is an irregular shape whose fill order is defined by a spiral on its enclosing rectangle rather than by row-major order on the shape itself.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:222:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:223:    maroons = [triple for triple in maroons if triple[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:224:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:226:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/20/code.py:227:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:25:#    - Example: if a blue chain goes upward from the target, a maroon sitting in a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:28:#      blue. A maroon beyond the tip of the chain is reachable, because the motion\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:57:#    - The generator always places distractor maroons inside blue-side pockets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:197:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:198:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:199:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:201:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:202:    chosen = [(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:246:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:247:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:248:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:249:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:250:    chosen = [(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:261:    Move the nearest legally reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:264:    - Orange floor carries scattered maroon tokens, while the target is the usual 3x3 green block with one red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/44/code.py:269:    - Sideways turns out of a blue cell are illegal, so maroons in side pockets touching a blue ray are not reachable; reachable maroons are ranked by directed distance and then fill the target in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:23:#      Inside that square, placement is no longer row-major. The moved maroons follow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:26:#      If reachable maroons exceed the square capacity, the next maroons do not stay\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:31:#      old task with 12 reachable maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:33:#      this combo with a 4x4 square and 19 reachable maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:35:#        surrounding spill ring, and only the still-later maroons would remain outside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:36:#      this combo with a 5x5 square and 11 reachable maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:60:#    - \"overflow maroons just stay put\" is invalid. The solver must erase not only the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:61:#      maroons moved inside the square, but also the extra selected maroons moved onto\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:66:#      non-destination, non-maroon color in the whole grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:76:#    - Source maroons and distractors are sampled only from floor cells, never from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:92:#    - The generator also keeps source maroons off the spill ring in the input, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:97:#      floor, wall, green square, red anchor, maroon tokens.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:102:#    - Non-overflow samples are forced to be partial fills (at least 6 maroons and at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:105:#      extra maroons is capped to a small visible band so the spill ring activates\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:280:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into a variable-size square, and spill any excess onto the square's outer ring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:283:    - Orange floor cells may be partitioned by magenta walls, with maroon tokens scattered on reachable and unreachable floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:287:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the square, traversing only floor and maroon cells, then rank reachable maroons by BFS distance, row, and column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:288:    - Fill the square first along a clockwise inward spiral. If more ranked maroons remain after the square is full, continue by placing them on the one-cell-thick ring immediately outside the square in clockwise perimeter order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:289:    - Every moved maroon is erased from its source cell back to floor; unreachable maroons and any maroons beyond the supported spill ring remain in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:292:    - The solver must recover both the square size and the two-stage write geometry. The square size sets the internal capacity, while overflow activates a second visible path just outside the square instead of leaving extra reachable maroons on the floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:305:    reachable_maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:306:    reachable_maroons = [item for item in reachable_maroons if item[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:307:    reachable_maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:309:    inner_count = min(len(fill_path), len(reachable_maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:310:    overflow_count = min(len(spill_order), max(0, len(reachable_maroons) - inner_count))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/54/code.py:312:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in reachable_maroons[:moved_total]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:153:def _old_bfs_ranked_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dest_set: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:298:    Move the closest maroon pixels that are directly visible through the frame openings into the central 3×3 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:302:    - The frame is mostly solid, but some non-corner side cells are single-cell openings; maroon pixels are scattered outside the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:306:    - That first blocking cell contributes only if it is maroon, so a frame opening exposes at most one candidate on that line while a wall cell blocks the ray immediately.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:310:    - The puzzle is about line of sight through explicit rectangular-frame openings, not about general corridor connectivity. A maroon pixel may still be reachable after exiting an opening, but if it requires a turn or sits behind another blocker on the same ray, it stays where it is.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/2/code.py:388:    ranked_old = _old_bfs_ranked_maroons(base, dest_set)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D14/1/code.py:63:#       - the pipe network is entirely cyan/8, with no grey or maroon helper colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:15:#    are directly adjacent to that block. Reachable maroon cells are found by BFS from the block's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:19:#      input full grid contains a 7x7 framed region plus extra outside maroons;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:22:#      after moving the closest reachable maroons into the block, the result is cropped to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:33:#    - Unreachable maroons can survive in the full grid but vanish from the final answer purely\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:44:#    hidden. Reachable maroons are visibly the ones inside the frame; outside maroons disappear\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:47:#    The three layers do not overlap: the block uses green/red, the channel uses orange/maroon, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:153:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the central 3x3 block, then crop to the enclosing frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:156:    - The canvas contains orange floor, scattered maroon tokens, a unique red center inside a 3x3 green block,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:158:    - The frame is not adjacent to the block: a 1-2 cell orange channel separates them, and maroons may appear\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:162:    - Flood-fill from passable cells adjacent to the 3x3 block through orange/maroon cells; maroons reached by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:164:    - Sort reachable maroons by distance to the block, breaking ties by row then column, and place the closest\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:169:    Key insight: The magenta border now defines both connectivity and the crop boundary; only maroons inside the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/16/code.py:268:    # Independent expectation: only maroons in the inner channel are reachable because the frame is closed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/9/code.py:25:#    - Replace the single maroon source class with multicolor single-pixel sources. This combo\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/9/code.py:39:#      dist 0-1 -> maroon(9), dist 2-3 -> gray(5), dist 4+ -> yellow(4).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/9/code.py:47:#    - The original floor-color inference relied on maroon being the only non-structural color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:19:      - floor/wall/maroon color roles stay the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:21:      - reachability still uses 4-connected BFS through floor+maroon cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:22:      - each destination still fills in row-major order with its owned maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:25:      - the mapping is many:many: many maroons may feed many blocks, and a block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:26:        competes with the others for shared maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:44:      distractors: optional unreachable maroons that remain in place\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:49:      - one BFS distance map ranks all reachable maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:50:      - the first k maroons fill that single container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:54:      - every maroon compares all reachable containers and is owned by the nearest\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:55:      - each container fills only from its owned maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:57:      - suppose a maroon lies in the central corridor and is reachable from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:81:    - original global `maroons[:k]` slice is invalid because each container has\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:88:      - merely selecting contested maroons is not enough, because the output only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:92:        input maroons than it actually owns after competition\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:94:        \"every container uses every reachable maroon independently\" reading\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:100:      - maroons are sampled only from floor cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:106:      - at least two containers receive contested maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:108:        maroons are owned by another container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:372:    Route reachable maroon pixels into several 3x3 destination blocks around red centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:375:    - The board is an 11x11 floor-and-wall maze with scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:379:    - For every destination block, compute BFS reachability through floor/maroon cells, stopping at walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:380:    - Each reachable maroon is owned by the nearest destination block; equal distances break by center row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:381:    - Every block sorts only its owned maroons by distance and writes them into its own 3x3 cells in row-major order, erasing the moved sources back to floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:385:    - Shared corridors create maroons that more than one block can reach, so you must compare several BFS frontiers first and only then refill each block from its assigned pool.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:408:    owned_maroons = [[] for _ in containers]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:414:        owned_maroons[owner].append((int(dists[owner][r, c]), r, c))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:417:        owned_maroons[idx].sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/10/code.py:418:        chosen = owned_maroons[idx][: len(dest_cells)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D13/2/code.py:24:#   L-shapes whose corner is exactly the companion dot.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D13/2/code.py:53:# - Candidate L-shapes are rejected if their output cells overlap another line's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D13/2/code.py:67:# - Outputs are built from non-overlapping L-shapes only; no dense criss-cross\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D13/2/code.py:149:      of an L-shape, and the same period is replayed on the orthogonal axis from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:16:#    with a left-hand rule. Maroons on the walked route move inward; maroons in side branches stay put.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:25:# 5. Visual observability: every valid sample includes at least one maroon in a branch that BFS could reach\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:188:    Pull maroon tokens from the left-hand wall-follow route of a maze into the 3x3 block around the red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:198:    - Collect maroons encountered on that traced route, erase them from their source cells, then fill the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:202:      so branch maroons that flood-fill could reach still remain in place unless the left-hand trace actually passes through them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:216:    maroons = [(r, c) for r, c in trace_cells if int(grid[r, c]) == MAROON]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:217:    k = min(len(DEST_CELLS), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/21/code.py:219:    for r, c in maroons[:k]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/1/code.py:402:    - Background cells stay empty; non-background cells form 3x3 tokens plus a cyan/grey/maroon pipe network whose junction rows can be read in two ways.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/8/code.py:78:#    - Extra noise is limited to small lines/L-shapes/blocks whose local degree\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/6/code.py:18:#    - The opening direction is still the corner it touches: NW / NE / SE / SW.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/6/code.py:41:#    - Wide bands can form an L-shaped front (size 3), so lockstep grouping must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/8/code.py:23:      - 一个蓝色 L 形块位于列 6 左侧，且其 bbox 中心离列 6 比离行 9 更近，所以它绕列 6 左右镜像\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:14:#    Example corridor: dest -> orange -> maroon A -> maroon B -> orange -> maroon C.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:15:#    Original dd6b8c4b treats maroon as passable, so A/B/C are all reachable in one BFS.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:23:#    - `passable = {floor, 9}` is no longer valid: maroon must block flood-fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:25:#      every collected maroon, so distances must be recomputed iteratively.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:26:#    - \"There is a passable start next to the destination\" is no longer guaranteed: a maroon can\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:27:#      sit directly at the opening, so the solver must allow direct-adjacent maroon targets even\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:34:#    marks hard obstacles, and maroon chains visibly sit inside the tunnels they block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:40:#    because some moved maroons are not initially exposed; they appear to come from behind others.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:43:#    the original \"floor+maroon are both passable\" ranking. The generator therefore measures the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:102:def _maroon_candidates(grid: np.ndarray, dest_cells: list[tuple[int, int]], dest_set: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:144:        candidates = _maroon_candidates(work, dest_cells, dest_set)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:157:    return [(r, c) for _dist, r, c in _maroon_candidates(np.asarray(grid, dtype=int), dest_cells, dest_set)[:max_take]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:161:    \"\"\"Reference helper for the original dd6b8c4b connectivity model: floor+maroon are passable.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:199:    Collect maroon tokens into the 3x3 target one at a time, recomputing reachability after each pick.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:202:    - Orange is the only traversable background; magenta walls and maroon tokens are both solid blockers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/19/code.py:207:    - At each step, consider maroon tokens touching that flood region (or touching the destination directly),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:11:  and maroon rectangular pass-through blocks (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:27:  diamonds, and may include 0-3 maroon pass-through rectangles that widen one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:36:  maroon blocks are unchanged in meaning.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:37:- `_trace_wire` assumes a wire may enter a maroon rectangle and must leave from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:199:    Follow one wire until its far endpoint, passing straight through maroon blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:269:    - Background cells surround several vertical cyan wire channels, sometimes widened by maroon rectangles, with 3x3 solid or X tokens sitting two cells beyond channel endpoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:395:    \"\"\"Attempt to place one straight pass-through maroon rectangle.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/5/code.py:48:#    - 三个碰撞点在模板中呈 L 形分布, 混色局部之间只有留白或原色线段, 不会糊成一团.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D6/1/code.py:11:#       - a bottom-anchored basin network with a left wall, a low L-shaped divider, and a taller divider;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:24:#   original: 5-pixel plus -> phase tile -> always 16x16 lattice -> centered 6x6 maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:25:#   variant:  5-pixel plus -> phase tile -> 15x15 lattice -> centered 6x6 maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:62:# - The output still has only two layers: a repeated orange/black lattice and a centered maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:69:#   color; output uses only black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:121:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a variable-size periodic lattice whose side length is set by the glyph's pixel count, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D5/1/code.py:131:    - Fill that canvas by tiling the phase tile, then place a centered 6x6 maroon stamp made from a 2x2 tiling of the original glyph.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:9:#    - solver 仍先从目标块外侧相邻的可通行单元做 flood-fill, 只把能通过 floor/maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:31:#      1. 候选排序从 `maroons.sort()` 改成按 `(-dist,row,col)`。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:45:#    - 通过限制 total maroon 数量与墙样式, 保持版面稀疏, 避免目标块附近过度拥挤。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:47:#    - 没有新增颜色语义。所有变化仍是 maroon 在 floor 与目标块之间移动。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:162:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:163:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:164:    return dest_cells, fill_order, floor, maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:170:    dest_cells, fill_order, floor, maroons = _reachable_analysis(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:173:        maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:175:        maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:178:    k = min(len(write_order), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:179:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:192:    Move the outermost reachable maroon pixels into the central 3x3 block, filling it from bottom-right backward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:196:    - Magenta walls may carve corridors around that block, and maroon tokens are scattered on floor cells outside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:199:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination, moving only through floor or maroon cells, to find reachable maroon candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:201:    - Remove the chosen sources and place the moved maroons into the destination in reverse row-major order, starting at the lower-right corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/4/code.py:204:    - The same wall-gated reachability test from the original task still decides which maroons are eligible, but both downstream directions are inverted: selection prefers the farthest candidates and writing prefers the bottom-right end of the block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:20:      - Keep the original 2x2 maroon stamp of the 3x3 glyph, so the stamp is still 6x6.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:36:    - Overwriting lattice cells with maroon is still safe because the original task already allowed the stamp to cover the lattice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:43:    - A left/right or top/bottom shift is immediately visible because the maroon stamp is large and contrasts with the orange/black lattice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:94:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice and place the maroon 2x2 stamp at a location derived from the glyph's input position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:104:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2, recolor its True cells to maroon, and treat that as a 6x6 stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/0/code.py:108:    - The glyph's shape still chooses the lattice phase, but the glyph's position in the 6x6 input now also encodes where the maroon stamp belongs on the 16x16 output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:22:#      pixel, green around it, orange floor, optional magenta wall barriers, and maroon tokens on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:24:#    - Reachability is unchanged: only maroons connected to the destination through a 4-neighbor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:25:#      flood-fill over floor+maroon cells are eligible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:27:#      1) source ranking order = row-major scan over reachable maroons, i.e. sort by (row, col);\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:31:#      reachable maroons = {(1,8),(2,2),(8,1),(9,9),...}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:34:#      then places the moved maroons down the first column of the target before moving right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:35:#    - Because the task always moves k = min(9, reachable_count) maroons, there is an unavoidable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:37:#      * if reachable_count > 9, the source ranking is visible because some reachable maroons stay\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:39:#      * if reachable_count < 9, the column-major fill is visible, but every reachable maroon moves,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:55:#    - The original `maroons.sort()` encoded distance ranking directly. That assumption is replaced\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:56:#      with sorting reachable maroons by coordinates only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:57:#    - Floor-color inference still needs at least one visible non-maroon ring-adjacent cell. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:63:#    - Source maroons are sampled only from reachable floor cells outside the destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:70:#    - Scan-order source selection is visible through which reachable maroons remain on the floor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:74:#    - Walls still provide clear corridor structure, so reachable and unreachable maroons remain\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:78:#      among visible maroons and the fill trajectory inside the fixed 3x3 target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:89:#      and at least one visible non-maroon neighbor color around the target for floor inference.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:152:    assert cand_ring, \"ring around destination must contain at least one visible non-maroon color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:229:    Move reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 target around the unique red center, ranking by scan position and filling by columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:236:    - Flood-fill from passable cells adjacent to the destination through floor and maroon cells to determine which maroon pixels are reachable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:237:    - Ignore path distance when ordering those reachable maroons: sort them only by row first, then column, erase the first up to nine source cells, and place those maroons into the destination in column-major order from the top-left.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:238:    - Destination cells beyond the moved count keep their original green/red colors, and unreachable maroons remain unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/5/code.py:241:    - The problem separates eligibility from placement: walls still decide which maroons can move, but once reachability is known the source order is a global scan order while the destination uses a different, column-first traversal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/17/code.py:26:#   1. 输入左上角附近有一个红十字：水平轴 r=1、垂直轴 c=1；一个绿色 L 形 seed 只在右下象限。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:16:#   structure is the 6x6 maroon stamp made by tiling the glyph 2x2: instead of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:21:#   In the source task, a plus glyph always produced the same centered maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:23:#   but its 6x6 maroon overlay starts at (0,0). Likewise an H still decodes to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:40:#   Overlap with the orange/black lattice is intentional and safe because maroon is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:43:#   The maroon overlay is large and isolated, so moving it from center to a corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:118:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a 16x16 periodic lattice with the motif stamped in maroon at a glyph-specific corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:128:    - Tile the input glyph 2x2 into a 6x6 maroon stamp, then place that stamp in a corner chosen by glyph type rather than at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D9/1/code.py:131:    - The input object still serves as a code for two output attributes: its contour determines the lattice phase, and that same contour class now also chooses which corner receives the maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:8:# - Baseline dd6b8c4b: the magenta barrier hugs the 3x3 green/red destination. Reachable maroons are found by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:9:#   floor BFS from cells immediately outside the block; maroons trapped behind the wall are ignored and stay put.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:14:# - D18/2 change: blocked maroons are not static distractors. Each trapped maroon sits in a sealed 1-cell pocket\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:17:#   recompute which maroons are reachable from the center block and fill the block by distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:18:# - Example trace: a maroon in the left-upper pocket at (3,1) is surrounded by wall on all four sides, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:20:#   is open, the maroon follows the frame around the top-left corner to the top opening at (0,5). From that new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:27:# - Pockets are single-cell chambers, so each moved maroon has a unique origin. Openings are one cell wide and are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:29:# - The generator enforces 2-3 moving maroons, at least one moved maroon that later fills the center block, at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:30:#   least one moved maroon that remains visible at an opening, and a wall-path length threshold. This prevents the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:36:# - Original assumption: unreachable maroons can be ignored forever. Broken by D18/2. Now they may become reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:38:# - Original assumption: clearing only the chosen reachable source cells is sufficient. Broken because moved maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:41:#   1. Every trapped maroon is adjacent to at least one wall cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:43:#   3. Different trapped maroons are assigned distinct nearest openings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:51:# - Reachable source maroons are sampled only from orange floor cells that are not pockets and not opening slots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:55:#   is the D14 part. They can also see maroons disappear from sealed side pockets and reappear on border openings,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:62:#   a handful of isolated pocket/source maroons. No region carries multiple kinds of markup on top of each other.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:63:# - Because pockets are tiny and sparse, the output does not become cluttered even when one moved maroon remains on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:64:#   the frame while other maroons fill the center block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:68:#   behavior, if at least two blocked maroons actually move along the frame, and if the moved maroons exhibit both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:187:def _move_blocked_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:198:    maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:199:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:200:    for r, c in maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:240:def _select_reachable_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:245:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:246:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:247:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:248:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:249:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:250:    return maroons, chosen\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:254:    maroons, chosen = _select_reachable_maroons(grid, dest_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:255:    _ = maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:266:    Route trapped maroons along a detached border frame, then use the closest reachable maroons to fill the center block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:271:    - Some maroons are ordinary reachable floor tokens, while others sit inside tiny sealed pockets attached to the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:274:    - First, detect maroons that are unreachable from the center through orange/maroon floor travel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:275:    - Each such blocked maroon moves along the connected magenta frame to the nearest valid side-center opening.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:276:    - After all blocked maroons relocate, recompute reachability and move the closest reachable maroons into the 3x3 block in row-major order, erasing the selected source positions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:291:    staged, _ = _move_blocked_maroons(grid, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:292:    _maroons, chosen = _select_reachable_maroons(staged, dest_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:339:    staged, moved = _move_blocked_maroons(np.asarray(grid, dtype=int), dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:340:    _maroons, chosen = _select_reachable_maroons(staged, dest_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/51/code.py:398:    staged_probe, moved_probe = _move_blocked_maroons(probe, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/35/code.py:75:#      insets, or L-shapes. Only a handful of interior anomalies are injected,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/20/code.py:15:#      * 输入: 左上有蓝色 L 形贴着一条竖红线, 更右下还有一条横红线和一个孤立红点, 后两者附近为空。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:16:#      green 3x3 target block and moves through floor/maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:48:#    - At least one blocked mouth exists, and at least four maroons lie in the 8-only reachable set.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:162:    maroons = [\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:167:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:169:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:170:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:181:    Move the nearest 8-reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:192:      maroon pixels as passable and magenta as blocking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:193:    - Collect only maroon pixels reached by that 8-connected search.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:194:    - Sort reachable maroons by distance, then row, then column, and copy the closest ones into\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:250:    maroon_cells = {(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:251:    only8_maroons = maroon_cells & (reach8 - reach4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:258:        \"only8_maroons\": len(only8_maroons),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:260:        \"nearest_only8_dist\": min((int(dist8[r, c]) for r, c in only8_maroons), default=-1),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/28/code.py:292:    if metrics[\"only8_maroons\"] < FILL_RANGE[0] or metrics[\"output_diff\"] <= 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:27:      color: recolor foreground to maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:63:    - size 4 and size 5 motifs differ by obvious stroke thickness and by the size of the central maroon stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:67:    - there are only three output colors (black, orange, maroon), as in the original task\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:68:    - the maroon stamp occupies one centered block, while the lattice remains readable around it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:166:    Decode a 4x4 or 5x5 enlarged contour glyph into a larger-period orange lattice and stamp the glyph family back in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/0/code.py:176:    - Fill a black 28x28 canvas by repeating that phase tile, then place a 2x2 maroon copy of the original enlarged glyph at the canvas center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/32/code.py:289:    - Black regions may also contain isolated single-pixel noise specks in several other colors (for example red, green, yellow, teal, or maroon) rather than only blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:36:#   reachable maroons, so the destination can only accept a subset.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:39:#   maroon back to inferred floor\". All three are unsafe now. This solver uses a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:41:#   generator guarantees every maroon sits on an orange endpoint so erasing a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:64:    MAROON: 1,  # generator places maroons on orange corridor endpoints\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:166:def _rank_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, *, weighted: bool) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:186:    ranked = _rank_reachable_maroons(g, weighted=True)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:199:    Move the lowest-cost reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the unique red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:204:    - Orange and grey corridor cells are both traversable; scattered maroon pixels sit on corridor endpoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:207:    - Start from corridor cells adjacent to the destination block and search through orange, grey, and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:208:    - Entering orange or maroon costs 1, while entering grey costs 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:209:    - Rank reachable maroons by total path cost, breaking ties by row then column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:210:    - Move the best-ranked maroons into the destination in row-major order and erase their source cells back to orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:241:    weighted = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, weighted=True)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:242:    plain = _rank_reachable_maroons(grid, weighted=False)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:23:#      keeping the maroon phase glyph legible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:28:#    - Reusing the whole boolean motif as the center stamp would incorrectly recolor decoration cells to maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:37:#    - Both colors are chosen from non-special ARC colors excluding black, orange, and maroon; they are distinct.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:39:#    - Across examples, one input color controls the global orange lattice and the maroon core glyph, while the other\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:47:#    - The maroon phase stamp and the decoration layer are disjoint by construction, avoiding ambiguous overpainting.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:50:#      the phase color is interpreted structurally: its shape becomes the orange lattice code plus a maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/1/code.py:148:    - Tile the canonical glyph 2x2 in maroon at the center, and tile the other color's mask 2x2 as an additional\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88bcf3b4/D9/0/code.py:4:# 现在改为沿 bar 前进方向的正交方向做纯水平/纯垂直延伸；整体从 V 形退出改为 L 形退出。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D15/0/code.py:14:#   The output keeps the 16x16 size and the centered 6x6 maroon 2x2 stamp, but the orange/black carrier\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D15/0/code.py:28:#   The centered maroon overwrite remains safe because it intentionally sits on top of the lattice in both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D15/0/code.py:38:#   The output still has only two layers: a black/orange background lattice and a maroon central stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D15/0/code.py:42:#   maroon for the center stamp, exactly as in the seed task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D15/0/code.py:85:    Decode the 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 diagonal lattice with the motif stamped in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D15/0/code.py:96:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:25:#      with the same phase decode and centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:44:#    - Humans can compare the edge bars with the maroon 6x6 center stamp in the output and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:53:#      orange, and maroon only. Colors are role-based and unchanged from the original\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:156:    Read a border legend that encodes a contour glyph, then expand it into the same 16x16 phase lattice and centered maroon stamp as the original task family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:166:    - Tile the phase over a black 16x16 canvas, then stamp a 2x2 maroon tiling of the reconstructed glyph into the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D2/3/code.py:169:    - The input foreground no longer marks the glyph directly inside the field; it is a border template that must be read first, and only the reconstructed motif controls both the lattice phase and the central maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:23:#    - D13/2 then changes what happens when too few reachable maroons exist:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:24:#      the solver still ranks reachable maroons by BFS distance, but if fewer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:28:#      input square = 5x5, reachable maroons = 6.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:29:#      Old D6-only logic: place 6 maroons into the first 6 cells of the full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:31:#      Fused logic: 6 maroons need only a 3x3 square, so the output keeps only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:33:#      with maroon, leaves the remaining 3 cells green, and turns the removed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:47:#    - \"moved maroons fill exactly the visible input container\" is invalid;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:70:#    - Walls remain external; maroons remain on floor in the input, so objects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:75:#    - The only count-based step is human-visible: count the reachable maroons,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/36/code.py:92:#    - Assumption: there is at least 