output only moved reachable maroon tokens into the 3x3 target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:42:#    maroons, but its hidden BFS footprint becomes visible: every reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:44:#    unreachable maroon distractor turns blue(1). Example: if a maroon sits\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:45:#    behind a wall arm, original output left it maroon; new output recolors it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:47:#    maroons are still removed, but their cells now become trail color rather\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:51:#    reachable path/background, 1 means rejected maroon. This is enough to make\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:60:#    It also cannot assume all non-moved maroons stay maroon: unreachable ones\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:69:#    connected region from the target openings, while rejected blue maroons sit\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:71:#    visible because only the closest reachable maroons are transferred into the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:82:#    non-empty unreachable floor, and at least one unreachable maroon so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:240:    Move the nearest reachable maroon pixels into the center block, while exposing the reachability map.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:243:    - The board uses orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and a unique red center inside a 3x3 green destination block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:247:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells adjacent to the destination, using orange and maroon cells as the traversable medium.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/48/code.py:248:    - Sort reachable m