aroon stamp as in the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D8/0/code.py:135:    - Tile the recovered 3x3 glyph 2x2 and stamp its true cells in maroon inside the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D7/1/code.py:123:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a 16x16 periodic lattice with the motif stamped in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D7/1/code.py:133:    - Fill the 16x16 canvas with that phase tile, then stamp a 2x2 maroon tiling of the glyph into the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:19:#   - Step 2 overwrites the centered coarse 2x2 block with maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:22:#     orange coarse pixels expand to orange glyph tiles, and maroon coarse pixels expand to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:23:#     maroon glyph tiles. The final canvas is therefore 18x18.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:26:#     orange/black lattice -> stamp a flat 6x6 maroon 2x2 repetition at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:28:#     place a coarse 2x2 maroon block -> recursively replace every non-black coarse cell by a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:50:#   - The expanded output assumes coarse pixels use only black/orange/maroon, which main()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:55:#   - The centered coarse 2x2 maroon block occupies rows 2..3 and cols 2..3 of the 6x6 macro\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:56:#     raster, yielding a centered 6x6 maroon-bbox in the 18x18 final output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:67:#   - Colors remain structurally simple: orange marks phase-lattice cells, maroon marks the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:147:    - Build a coarse 6x6 lattice by tiling that phase tile and overwrite the centered coarse 2x2 block with maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:148:    - Expand each coarse pixel into a 3x3 child tile shaped like the input glyph: orange cells become orange glyph tiles, maroon cells become maroon glyph tiles, and black cells stay black.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:28:#    - 原题的 `maroons.sort()` 默认是最近优先；这里必须改成距离降序，否则 D3/0 不生效。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:35:#    - 生成器先在仅 floor 的距离图上选近层/远层候选，再把这些 floor 位置改成 maroon，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:47:#    - 新规则不引入新的颜色种类，只重排已有 maroon / green / red 的出现位置。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:169:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:170:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:171:    return dest_cells, fill_slots, floor, maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:177:    dest_cells, fill_slots, floor, maroons = _analyze_grid(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:180:        maroons.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], t[2]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:182:        maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:185:    k = min(len(target_slots), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:186:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:199:    Move the farthest reachable maroon pixels into a checkerboard subset of the 3x3 block around the lone red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:202:    - The board is an orange floor with optional magenta walls and scattered maroon source pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:206:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination, walking only through floor or maroon cells, and keep only reachable maroon pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:208:    - Move the selected maroons into the destination's row-major odd positions only, which forms a checkerboard pattern; the even positions keep their original green/red contents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/23/code.py:211:    - The walls still determine reachability, but the visible output now combines two independent cues: source removal prefers the outermost reachable maroons, and the target block only accepts them on alternating checkerboard cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/28/code.py:24:#     - 每个样例至少放 2 个假红装饰，且既可能是单点，也可能是短线/L 形，保证“同色干扰”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/2/code.py:25:#     - centered 6x6 maroon stamp made by 2x2 tiling the 3x3 glyph\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/2/code.py:43:#       -> stamp the centered maroon 2x2 motif\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/2/code.py:55:#   - stamping must happen after erasing; otherwise the erase step would clip maroon pixels and blur the two-stage logic.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/2/code.py:61:#   - the output keeps only black/orange/maroon, so the new effect is silhouette-based and clean.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/2/code.py:63:#   - only two layers remain in the lattice region (orange on black), plus the central maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/2/code.py:131:    - Erase the tiled lattice outside that window, then tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/0/code.py:17:#   shifts it by one column. The central 6x6 maroon stamp is unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/0/code.py:35:#   Phase shifts affect the whole background lattice while the central maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/0/code.py:95:    - Repeat that phase tile over a black 16x16 canvas using the chosen offset, then tile the original glyph 2x2 and recolor its true cells to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/14/code.py:146:    Key insight: The solver must recognize a broken rotationally symmetric cross from its asymmetric L-shaped fragment. Detection is done on the original input only, and each detected elbow is expanded to the unique full '+' centered at the same pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:14:#    The original task used a centered 3x3 destination and maroon tokens scattered anywhere on floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:16:#    Maroon sources are no longer interior speckles: every movable or distracting maroon lies on the outer border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:19:#    which maroons qualify, but now the candidate pool itself is visibly \"edge only\" and strongly asymmetric.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:22:#    positional change from a few examples. Border-only maroons are a strong visual cue, and the wall layout uses\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:26:#    - Collectible maroons are filtered to border cells only; interior maroons, if present, are ignored as sources.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:30:#    The chosen centers keep the full 5x5 wall frame in-bounds. Walls, destination cells, and border maroons occupy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:31:#    disjoint cell sets, and all source/distractor maroons are sampled only from floor border cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:33:#    In 2-4 examples, a solver can see that maroons only appear on the boundary and that the block sits off-center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:34:#    Which border maroons move is explained by visible corridors/openings rather than invisible bookkeeping.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:36:#    Each role has its own region: the 3x3 target, a magenta wall frame, and edge-only maroons. This avoids the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:39:#    No new color remapping is introduced. The only semantic change is positional: \"border maroons reachable through\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:184:    Move the nearest reachable border maroons into the off-center 3x3 block around the red pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:188:    - Maroon source pixels appear only on the outer border of the grid; some border maroons may be cut off by walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:191:    - Find the unique red cell, take its surrounding 3x3 as the destination, then flood-fill outward through floor and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:192:    - Only border maroons reached by that flood-fill are candidates; sort them by BFS distance, then row, then column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:196:    - The asymmetry comes from two places at once: candidate maroons live only on the border, and the target block sits closer to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:197:      some borders than others. Visible wall barriers decide which border sides can actually contribute maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:238:    maroons = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:243:            maroons.append((int(dist[r, c]), r, c))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:244:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:246:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/22/code.py:247:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:17:#      maroon stamp made by tiling the 3x3 glyph 2x2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:33:#      leaving the centered maroon stamp unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:44:#    - The centered 6x6 maroon stamp in output is unchanged and cannot conflict with generation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:50:#    - The output still has only two clean layers: periodic background and centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:53:#    - Colors are unchanged from the original task: orange/black for the lattice and maroon for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:91:    Turn the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice whose phase is shifted by the glyph placement, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/3/code.py:102:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/0/code.py:18:#      2. a centered 6x6 maroon stamp made by tiling the original 3x3 glyph 2x2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/0/code.py:31:#                  more separated lattice. The center 6x6 maroon H-stamp is unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/0/code.py:61:#    - Only two layers exist in the output: the periodic orange/black lattice and the central maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/0/code.py:66:#      Output still uses only black, orange, and maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/0/code.py:112:    Read the 3x3 contour glyph as both a phase-shape code and a period code, then build the repeated lattice with the glyph stamped in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/0/code.py:123:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon inside the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:23:#    - Reachability still uses 4-neighbor BFS through floor/maroon cells, but a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:24:#      maroon is moved only if it lies within the number of BFS layers unlocked\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:27:#      old: fixed 3x3, all reachable maroons compete for 9 cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:28:#      new 4x4: only distance<=1 maroons are moved, and output becomes 6x6.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:29:#      new 5x5: distance<=2 maroons are moved, and output becomes 9x9.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:34:#    - Generators force at least one moved maroon on the outermost unlocked BFS\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:35:#      layer and at least one farther reachable maroon that remains, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:50:#    - Distractor maroons are sampled outside the final expanded square so they\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:55:#    - The output visibly shows a larger green/maroon square, revealing that the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:57:#    - Farther reachable maroons remain on the floor, so the growth cutoff is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:62:#    - Walls and leftover maroons remain outside the final container, avoiding\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:72:#    - Each accepted grid must have at least one moved maroon on the last growth\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:73:#      layer and at least one still-reachable maroon beyond that layer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:82:#    - Assumption: leftover maroons outside the moved set are outside the final\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:199:    Grow a variable-size square container outward and move only the maroons reached within its growth depth.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:202:    - Orange floor contains optional magenta walls and scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:206:    - Flood-fill through floor and maroon cells from the square's outside edge, measuring 4-neighbor BFS distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:207:    - The square expands by a size-dependent number of rings: 4x4 grows by 1 ring, 5x5 grows by 2 rings. Move only the maroons within those unlocked BFS layers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:208:    - Erase moved maroons to floor, replace the expanded square by green, then write the collected maroons into that expanded square in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:225:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/41/code.py:226:    chosen = [(d, r, c) for d, r, c in maroons if d <= rounds]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:18:#       color: any single color except black(0), orange(7), maroon(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:23:#     stamp: the original 4x4 motif tiled 2x2 into an 8x8 maroon center block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:24:#     colors_used: black(0), orange(7), maroon(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:36:#        output       = repeat that 3x3 tile, then stamp a 6x6 maroon 2x2 copy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:40:#        output       = repeat that 4x4 tile on 16x16, then stamp an 8x8 maroon 2x2 copy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:76:#      maroon stamp. No extra markers or overlapping annotation channels are added.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:81:#      Output colors stay restricted to black/orange/maroon, exactly as in the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:168:    Decode the colored 4x4 contour motif into a 16x16 period-4 lattice and stamp a centered maroon 2x2 copy of that motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D6/2/code.py:178:    - Tile the original 4x4 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 8x8 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:27:#      6x6 maroon stamp made by tiling the 3x3 glyph 2x2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:54:#    - Center stamping still assumes the lattice can be overwritten by maroon on motif\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:64:#    - Humans can see the change directly: outside the maroon center, orange cells now\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:72:#      centered maroon overlay. The overlay is confined to a 6x6 block, so most of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:75:#    - Output colors stay limited to black(0), orange(7), and maroon(9). Orange marks the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:77:#      maroon marks the centered 2x2 glyph stamp. This structured reuse keeps the rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:103:    Turn the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice that uses the glyph itself as the orange phase tile, then stamp the glyph in maroon at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D1/2/code.py:113:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:19:#   with a red center and green ring, orange floor, magenta walls, and many maroon tokens outside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:22:#   2. Among reachable maroons, the chosen movers are ordered by Euclidean distance to the block center,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:31:# - Important difference from the original generator: if there are <= 9 reachable maroons, every reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:33:#   reachable maroons so the 9-cell capacity forces a visible keep-vs-move selection.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:37:# - Use 10-14 reachable maroons and at most 0-3 unreachable distractors. This is enough to expose the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:48:#   Broken by D3/2. The new solver must compute reachability by flood-fill but rank selected maroons by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:50:# - Original assumption hidden in the old generator: reachable maroon count can be 2-9.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:52:#   The new generator guarantees more reachable maroons than capacity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:57:# - The destination block is fixed at rows 4-6 and cols 4-6; source maroons are placed only on floor cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:64:# - Because only 9 of 10-14 reachable maroons move, some reachable maroons remain outside in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:73:# - Distractors are limited and optional. Most of the visual signal comes from the reachable maroons around\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:78:# - The green ring must stay passable; generator never replaces it with walls or maroons in the input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:169:def _reachable_maroons_from_center(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], np.ndarray, list[tuple[int, int]]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:172:    maroons = [\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:177:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:178:    return center, dist, maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:182:    center, _dist, maroons = _reachable_maroons_from_center(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:183:    ranked = sorted(maroons, key=lambda rc: (_euclid2(center, rc), rc[0], rc[1]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:188:    _center, dist, maroons = _reachable_maroons_from_center(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:189:    ranked = sorted(maroons, key=lambda rc: (int(dist[rc[0], rc[1]]), rc[0], rc[1]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:197:    maroons = [\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:202:    ranked = sorted(maroons, key=lambda rc: (int(dist[rc[0], rc[1]]), rc[0], rc[1]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:222:    center, dist_center, reachable = _reachable_maroons_from_center(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:247:    Move the selected reachable maroons into the centered 3x3 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:255:      and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:256:    - Keep only the reachable maroons, then rank them by Euclidean distance to the block center, breaking ties\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/6/code.py:258:    - Move up to nine ranked maroons into the destination block in row-major order and erase only those sources.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D3/2/code.py:16:#     - 原逻辑：若训练源图里有两个分开的 L 形，global fill 会跨整个 6x6 的行列范围补点，可能把两个对象混在一起。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D14/2/code.py:26:#      stamp one maroon 2x2 motif at the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D14/2/code.py:29:#      and the later bbox layer second -> stamp the union of the two 2x2 motifs in maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D14/2/code.py:46:#      maroon \"stamp\" idea is preserved by taking the union after 2x2 tiling.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D14/2/code.py:55:#    There are only two lattice colors plus black and the single maroon center stamp. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D14/2/code.py:151:    Decode two colored contour glyphs into stacked periodic lattices, then seal their combined motif as a centered maroon stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D14/2/code.py:161:    - Composite the two repeated layers so the later bbox in row-major order overwrites the earlier one, then stamp the 2x2-tiled union of both glyphs in maroon inside the centered 6x6 window.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/12/code.py:32:       an L-shaped red marker. Its corner is the anchor, and the payload reflects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/12/code.py:481:    - L-shaped red marker -> diagonal reflection\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:18:#    - Replace the single maroon source class with 2-3 token colors drawn from a small fixed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:25:#        distance order      = [(d0,blue), (d1,maroon), (d2,blue), (d3,yellow)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:26:#        grouped order       = [(blue,d0), (blue,d2), (yellow,d3), (maroon,d1)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:28:#      Original task would have written a uniform maroon row-major prefix; this combo instead\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:39:#    - `passable = {floor, 9}` breaks because movable tokens are no longer all maroon; now every\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/30/code.py:46:#    - Original floor inference from \"the only other color is maroon\" is unsafe with multi-color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D16/1/code.py:141:    - Fill a 16x16 canvas by tiling that phase with the legend-selected colors, then stamp a 2x2 maroon copy of the glyph in the centered 6x6 region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/0/code.py:96:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 into a 6x6 pattern and recolor its true cells to maroon at the exact center of the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:18:#   - Replace the old \"all reachable maroons are already passable, then sort once by distance\" rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:21:#       2. A maroon cell is collected when it sits on the current BFS frontier, i.e. it is 4-neighbor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:23:#       3. Collected maroons turn into floor, so the reachable floor region expands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:24:#       4. Repeat layer by layer until the 3x3 destination is full or no frontier maroons remain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:25:#   - This makes maroon cells behave like removable gate tokens instead of already-open corridor cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:29:#       * Treat floor and maroon as passable from the start.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:31:#       * Sort every reachable maroon by raw BFS distance and move the closest ones.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:34:#       * Just beyond that opening, one maroon gate blocks access to the first annulus.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:35:#       * After removing that gate, the first annulus becomes reachable; maroons sitting in that annulus\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:39:#       * Reachability is no longer static. A farther maroon that is \"close\" under the original solver\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:42:#         gate maroon that must be peeled away before the next depth becomes reachable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:48:#     maroons, so the solver must reason about both partial final-layer filling and nested unlocking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:49:#   - The generator prefers far-from-entry maroons in inner annuli and near-entry maroons in outer annuli,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:57:#   - The original assumption \"maroon is globally passable\" is no longer valid. The combo solver must BFS\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:68:#   - Gate maroons are reserved on floor cells known to be inside bounds and not in the destination block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:69:#   - Source maroons are sampled from disjoint floor-cell candidate sets; distractors, when used, are sampled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:73:#   - A human sees nested magenta frames with different opening sides, plus maroons clustered by depth.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:74:#   - The output effect is not just \"take the closest maroons\": inner gate tokens disappear first, then the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:346:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:347:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:348:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:349:    chosen = [(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[: len(dest_cells)]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:375:    Pull maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the red center by unlocking the nested frames layer by layer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:384:    - At each step, collect every maroon that lies on the current BFS frontier, in row-major order; the collected maroons become floor, which may open the next annulus.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:385:    - Continue outward layer by layer until the destination block is full or no frontier maroons remain, then place the collected maroons into the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/14/code.py:387:    Key insight: The nested magenta frames do not just filter static reachability. Their openings create a sequence of locked annuli, and maroon gates must be removed in BFS layers before farther maroons can even become candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/2/code.py:30:#      centered 6x6 maroon mark. Empty input cells map to all-black panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/2/code.py:59:#    - Panels are spatially disjoint, separated by black gutters, and maroon only appears\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D12/2/code.py:158:    - In the output mosaic, fill the corresponding 8x8 panel with that orange/black tile and stamp a 2x2 tiling of the glyph in maroon at the panel center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:22:#     stamp: still a 2x2 tiling of the original glyph recolored to maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:31:#     plus -> decode phase -> always build a 16x16 lattice -> stamp the 6x6 maroon motif at rows 5..10, cols 5..10\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:33:#     plus -> decode phase -> build a 12x12 lattice -> center the same 6x6 maroon stamp at rows 3..8, cols 3..8\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:34:#     H    -> decode phase -> build an 18x18 lattice -> center the same 6x6 maroon stamp at rows 6..11, cols 6..11\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:52:#   - Output placement is always legal because every canvas size is square and >= 12, while the maroon stamp is fixed at 6x6.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:57:#   - The new rule is visible because the whole output frame expands or shrinks by glyph type while the central maroon motif stays 6x6.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:61:#   - Only three output colors remain: black, orange, maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:62:#   - The maroon stamp stays in a dedicated centered block, separated from the outer lattice by several cells on every size class.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:120:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a glyph-sized periodic lattice and place a centered maroon stamp of the motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/0/code.py:130:    - Fill that square canvas by tiling the decoded phase tile, then center a 2x2 maroon tiling of the original glyph on top.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:17:#    The original task only moved reachable maroon tokens into the fixed 3x3 destination and erased\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:22:#    - within that region, the actual predecessor chains that carry chosen maroons back to the target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:35:#      chosen maroons back into floor. That no longer holds; reachable background must also change.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:40:#      reachable branch with no maroon source, so some explored cells remain yellow-only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:45:#    maroons are placed on isolated floor pockets outside the corridor network.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:48:#    untouched walls stay magenta, unreachable pockets stay orange/maroon, all reachable background\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:57:#    carries collected maroons\". The generator enforces both roles in every accepted sample.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:180:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:181:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < INF]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:182:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:184:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:185:    chosen = [(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:206:    Gather reachable maroon pixels into the central 3x3 block and visualize both the explored region and the transport routes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:209:    - The board contains orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and a fixed green 3x3 destination with one red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:210:    - Passable openings beside the destination lead into corridor-like floor regions; isolated floor pockets may hold unreachable distractor maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:213:    - Flood-fill from passable cells touching the destination, treating orange floor and maroon tokens as passable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:214:    - Rank reachable maroons by flood-fill distance, then by row and column; the closest ones fill the destination in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:215:    - In the output, every reachable floor cell becomes yellow to show the explored background, while the actual floor cells on each chosen source-to-destination parent chain are recolored teal; chosen source maroons themselves disappear back to orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:218:    - The fill order is still controlled by reachability and distance, but the fused variant exposes two nested BFS products: the full reachable background region and the narrower subset of floor cells that lie on the transport routes of the collected maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:20:#     old_center_rule: every true pixel of the 2x2 tiled glyph became maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:21:#     new_center_rule: maroon appears only where the tiled glyph overlaps the 3-period lattice seams\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:25:#     variant: for plus, only the 8 true pixels on rows {0,3} or cols {0,3} inside that 6x6 box become maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:29:#       which would collapse the stamp to zero maroon pixels\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:101:    - Tile the 3x3 glyph 2x2 into the centered 6x6 box, but recolor to maroon only where those glyph pixels also lie on the box's period-3 seam rows or seam columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:126:    maroon_mask = center & seam_mask\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:130:    out[r0 : r0 + center.shape[0], c0 : c0 + center.shape[1]][maroon_mask] = Color.MAROON\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:149:    maroon_count = int((center == Color.MAROON).sum())\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:150:    if maroon_count <= 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:19:#      keep only reachable maroons, sort them by BFS step distance, then place\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:20:#      the chosen maroons into the 3x3 block in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:23:#      1. Mark every reachable maroon with its BFS reachability information.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:24:#      2. Re-sort those marked maroons by Euclidean distance to the red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:34:#      only when there are more than 9 reachable maroons.  Then the top-9 set\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:35:#      itself can differ, changing which scattered maroons disappear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:38:#    - The generator forces >9 reachable maroons and requires the Euclidean\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:48:#    - \"only orange floor and maroon are passable\": unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:56:#    - Generator places maroons only on floor cells, never inside the 3x3 block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:59:#      sources, leftover reachable maroons, and distractors never overlap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:62:#    - A human can see the distinction because some maroons that are geometrically\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:64:#      farther maroon that stays behind.  The walls provide the visible reason\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:71:#      red center, maroon tokens.  No extra marks are added.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:73:#      barrier network, scattered maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:138:def _mark_reachable_maroons(grid: np.ndarray, dest_cells: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:147:def _sort_marked_maroons(marked: list[tuple[int, int, int]], center_r: int, center_c: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:165:    Pull reachable maroons into the central 3x3 block, but separate marking,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:175:    - Phase 1 marks every maroon that is reachable through 4-connected floor or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:176:      maroon cells starting from passable cells adjacent to the target block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:177:    - Phase 2 reorders only those marked maroons by Euclidean distance to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:179:    - Phase 3 moves the first nine (or fewer) maroons from that Euclidean list:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:185:      longer depends on corridor length.  A maroon that is geometrically close\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:186:      to the center can outrank a path-shorter maroon if walls force a detour.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:195:    marked = _mark_reachable_maroons(grid, dest_cells)   # phase 1: mark\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/46/code.py:196:    ordered = _sort_marked_maroons(marked, cr, cc)       # phase 2: sort\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:21:#     - the old output had one 6x6 maroon stamp at the center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:32:#     - place one 6x6 maroon plus-stamp at center top-left (5,5)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:36:#     - place the same 6x6 maroon plus-stamp four times at the quadrant-style slot origins\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:39:#     - the maroon foreground is no longer a single central event; it forms a regular 2x2 arrangement\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:59:#   - four maroon copies are obvious in 2-3 examples even when the glyph is symmetric\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:62:#   - maroon only overlays the phase lattice and never another stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:65:#   - colors remain structurally simple: orange/black lattice plus maroon stamps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:117:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a 16x16 periodic lattice with the motif stamped multiple times in maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/1/code.py:127:    - Tile the original 3x3 glyph into a 6x6 stamp and place that maroon stamp at every slot of a regular 2x2 stamp lattice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/4/code.py:14:      in the center window with fixed maroon(9). This variant transfers the visible input\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/4/code.py:20:    - Original behavior at the last step: center glyph pixels become maroon regardless of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/4/code.py:60:      maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/4/code.py:61:    - Excluding maroon ensures generated samples do not collapse back to the original fixed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/4/code.py:62:      maroon behavior, so the D4 change stays observable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:20:#        source task: center 6x6 receives a 2x2 maroon tiling of the glyph\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:21:#        this variant: center 6x6 is forced to pure black, and one 3x3 maroon copy of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:24:#        old flow  : decode plus -> periodic lattice -> maroon plus tiled at center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:26:#                    -> stamp maroon plus at (0,0), (0,13), (13,0), (13,13)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:33:#      corners carry the same maroon glyph. This is easy to compare across examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:38:#    - The old code assumed the only maroon overlay lived in a centered 6x6 block made by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:53:#      black, and the maroon glyph migrates to all four corners. Because the lattice still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:58:#      center, maroon stamps only in corners. No region carries multiple competing marks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:61:#    - Colors remain black/orange/maroon only in the output. Maroon still signals the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:108:    Decode the colored 3x3 contour glyph into a 16x16 periodic lattice whose center becomes a black void and whose corners carry maroon glyph stamps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:118:    - Erase the centered 6x6 zone to pure black, then stamp one maroon copy of the glyph into each of the four 3x3 corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D3/3/code.py:178:    # corner must contain at least one maroon pixel from the glyph stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/14/code.py:50:#    - Large black foreground objects remain simple bands / rectangles / L-shapes so that the new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D4/3/code.py:21:#     - Source motif: a 2x2 logical L-shape with exactly 3 foreground cells, one of them red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D4/3/code.py:31:#         so the target quadrant shows three copies arranged in the same L-shape, each copy itself\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D4/3/code.py:53:#     - The L-shaped 2x2 logical motif guarantees visible holes/gaps, so the result is not mistaken for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D4/3/code.py:237:    \"\"\"Return a 2x2 logical L-shape with one red cell and two distinct extra colors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:67:     1. the mover is visibly L-shaped rather than square;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:69:     3. the red goal is a larger docking frame with an L-shaped blue notch, and reachable outputs keep that frame\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:28:     3. The destination is a red docking frame whose inner cavity is an L-shaped blue notch\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D15/1/code.py:14:#    这个变体把单像素替换成 3x3 的同色 L 形记号；颜色仍然代表调色板颜色，但排序距离不再默认从最近边界测，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:5:# 编码的小型 L 形图例，同色图例指示该颜色阻挡对应的转向偏好（CCW 或 CW）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:12:#      其中 3 个同色像素构成一个 L 形符号：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:20:#      之一为真；本题中两者都为真，若底边颜色 4 的 L 形是 CCW，则转到上口，否则转到下口。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:48:#    - 每个图例条目就是一个 2x2 的单色 L 形，背景仍是原背景色 7；不会引入额外装饰噪声。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:60:#    - 假设 B：每个图例颜色在底边形成一个 4 连通、3 像素、2x2 bbox 的 L 形。生成器严格保证。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D14/0/code.py:116:    \"\"\"Read 2x2 bottom-edge L-shape symbols as color -> {ccw,cw}.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:23:    - Original: two L-shaped outside pieces could never exist, because two L-shaped holes were forbidden.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:24:    - Variant: two L-shaped holes may both exist. One hole touches a red wall marker, the other touches blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D1/0/code.py:34:    - 原逻辑：两个 L 形洞分别对应红/绿两个外部 L 形 piece。solver 先枚举每个 piece 的所有 D4 变体，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D1/0/code.py:36:    - 变体逻辑：两个 L 形洞的洞边墙像素分别染成红/绿。solver 先看到“红洞边 -> 红 piece、绿洞边 -> 绿 piece”，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D9/2/code.py:17:#     - 例：原任务里 3 格 L 形洞会变成 2x2 或 3x3 块拼出的 L 形精灵。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D10/0/code.py:19:#    8-neighbor depth differ. Example: in an L-shaped region,