py:30:#       - D18 changes only the handling of originally unreachable maroons; reachable-source ranking and destination filling stay as in the seed task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:33:#     - pockets are only one cell each, so each moved maroon has a single unambiguous origin.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:34:#     - generator enforces both branches: at least one blocked maroon moves to an inner opening and at least one moves to an outer opening.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:37:#       - \"unreachable maroons can be ignored for selection\" is no longer safe.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:38:#       - clearing only chosen reachable maroons is no longer sufficient because blocked maroons now relocate before ranking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:39:#       - BFS only on floor+maroon still works for final selection, but it must run after the wall-motion stage.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:41:#       - blocked maroons must touch at least one wall cell; generator guarantees this by using pocket cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:43:#       - no two blocked maroons may need the same opening; generator validates distinct nearest targets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:45:#     - destination, inner ring, outer frame, pocket connectors, openings, and maroons are all placed on fixed non-overlapping cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:46:#     - reachable source maroons are sampled only from floor cells that are not pockets and not opening slots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:48:#     - the only new visual event is \"sealed-pocket maroons jump to wall gaps\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:206:def _move_blocked_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:227:    maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:228:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:229:    for r, c in maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:264:    Move blocked maroon pixels to the nearest wall opening, then fill the center block with the closest reachable maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:268:    - Magenta walls form an inner ring, an outer frame, and small sealed side pockets containing some maroon pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:271:    - First, any maroon already reachable from the destination through floor/maroon cells stays in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:272:    - Any maroon trapped behind the magenta walls instead travels along the connected wall framework to the nearest open side-center slot.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:273:    - After that relocation, recompute reachability and move the closest reachable maroons into the 3x3 destination in row-major order, erasing them from their source cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:276:    - The critical change is not how reachable maroons are ranked, but that blocked maroons are no longer static distractors: the wall network itself routes them to visible openings, and inner openings can turn them into new candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:288:    staged, _ = _move_blocked_maroons(grid, cr, cc, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:291:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(staged == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:292:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:293:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:295:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:296:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:338:    staged, moved = _move_blocked_maroons(np.asarray(grid, dtype=int), CENTER_R, CENTER_C, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:340:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(staged == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:341:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:342:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:343:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[: min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:379:    staged_probe, moved_probe = _move_blocked_maroons(probe, CENTER_R, CENTER_C, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:411:    staged, moved = _move_blocked_maroons(inp, CENTER_R, CENTER_C, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/3/code.py:87:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/3/code.py:131:    - Away from the legend, each marker color appears either as an L-shaped diagonal corner pair or as a solid 2x2 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/2/code.py:83:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:23:#      maroon tokens. Output still moves the closest reachable maroon tokens\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:27:#      old: 3x3 block -> cap 9 -> 12 reachable maroons still fill only 9 cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:28:#      new: 4x4 block -> cap 16 -> the same 12 reachable maroons fill 12 cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:29:#      new: 4x4 block + 19 reachable maroons -> only the closest 16 move, 3 stay.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:34:#      reachable maroons remain outside once the square is full.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:55:#      fill completely while nearby reachable maroons remain on the floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:59:#    - Walls remain outside the square; maroons remain on floor cells, so layers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:68:#      overflow cases (reachable maroons > capacity) so the D6 change is active.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:175:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into a variable-size square container marked by a red corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:178:    - Orange floor contains optional magenta walls and scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:182:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells touching the square, traversing only floor and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:183:    - Sort reachable maroon pixels by BFS distance, then by row and column, and move as many as fit into the square in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:184:    - Moved maroons are erased back to floor; any extra reachable or unreachable maroons remain where they are.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:187:    - The red pixel is no longer the center of a fixed 3x3 target. The solver must first recover the full red/green square, because its area determines how many maroons can be collected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:198:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:199:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:200:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:202:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:203:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/4/code.py:8:#     - 网格尺寸、左下角竖直图例、L 形对角标记、可选 2x2 方块、可选 distractor 都保持原题风格。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/4/code.py:11:#     - L 形标记不再是输出的一部分，而是“临时施工线”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/4/code.py:92:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:19:      - orange floor, optional magenta walls, maroon movable tokens\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:21:      - reachability is still decided by 4-connected flood-fill through floor/maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:22:      - each container still fills in row-major order using its closest assigned maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:26:      - a maroon reachable from both containers is assigned to the nearer container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:40:      sources: maroon cells placed on floor cells owned by one of the two containers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:41:      distractors: optional maroon cells unreachable from both containers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:46:      - sort all reachable maroons by that one distance\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:50:      - for each maroon, compare the two distances and assign the maroon to the nearer block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:51:      - inside each block, sort only that block's assigned maroons and fill its own 3x3 cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:53:      - if a central maroon can reach both blocks, the old solver would have no notion of competition\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:70:    - original single BFS distance map assumes every reachable maroon belongs to the same target; invalid now\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:71:    - original `chosen = maroons[:k]` assumes one global quota; invalid now because each block needs its own quota\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:78:      - chosen maroon sources and distractors are sampled from floor cells only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:85:      - at least one moved maroon comes from such an overlap region, so multi-target ownership is exercised\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:181:    Route reachable maroon pixels into multiple 3×3 destination blocks around red centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:184:    - bg = orange floor, optional magenta walls, scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:188:    - For each destination block, compute reachability through floor/maroon cells, stopping at walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:189:    - Every reachable maroon is assigned to the nearest destination block; equal distances go to the earlier center in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:190:    - Inside each block, assigned maroons are ranked by distance to that block and fill the block in row-major order; moved maroons are erased back to floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:211:    owned_maroons = [[] for _ in containers]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:217:        owned_maroons[owner].append((int(dists[owner][r, c]), r, c))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:220:        owned_maroons[idx].sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:221:        chosen = owned_maroons[idx][: len(dest_cells)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D9/0/code.py:19:#    example, always places L-shapes at TL and BR, so the painted region is always\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D9/0/code.py:97:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:24:#      Variant: an L-shape might occupy {(5,5),(6,5),(7,5),(5,6),(5,7)}. If k=4,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:64:#    - Assumption: at least one passable floor/maroon cell touches the container so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:92:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the irregular green container attached to the unique red anchor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:95:    - The board still uses orange floor, optional magenta walls, and scattered maroon tokens.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:99:    - Maroon pixels that can reach the container through floor/maroon cells are candidates, with walls blocking traversal exactly as before.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:100:    - Rank reachable maroons by BFS distance to the container, then place the closest ones into the container's own cells in row-major order, skipping positions outside the shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:101:    - Any moved maroon source is erased back to floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:153:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:154:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:155:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:157:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:158:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/24/code.py:63:#    - The frame border is uniformly one color and the informative dots occupy only a thin L-shaped guide structure near\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D9/2/code.py:52:#     - marker pixels remain protected so the L-shapes are still readable after filling\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D9/2/code.py:101:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D9/2/code.py:236:      appear elsewhere either as a diagonal pair of L-shaped corners or as one solid 2x2 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D9/2/code.py:247:    the very diagonal that carries the two L-shaped anchors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:16:#    Reachable maroon tokens are still gathered by flood-fill reachability and distance, but now the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:18:#    recolored teal (8) in the output. The maroon source cell itself still disappears to orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:40:#    corridor tree at exactly one 4-neighbor so no loops are created. Distractor maroons are placed in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:153:    Pull reachable maroon pixels into the central 3×3 block and leave teal transport trails behind.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:156:    - The canvas uses orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and a fixed green 3×3 target with one red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:157:    - Floor openings beside the target connect into corridors; only maroons reachable through those corridors participate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:160:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells touching the target, treating orange floor and maroon tokens as passable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:161:    - Sort reachable maroons by flood-fill distance, then by row and column; the closest ones fill the target in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:162:    - Each chosen source maroon disappears back to orange, and every orange floor cell on its discovered route to the target is recolored teal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:181:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:182:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:183:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:185:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:186:    chosen = [(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:3:# Change: L 形 3 像素角标记，位于外接矩形的对角两端（共 6 像素）；另有 2x2 实心方块变体... → 十字形标记\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:25:      - expected L-shaped anchors at bbox corners\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/3/code.py:3:# Change: L 形 3 像素角标记，位于外接矩形的对角两端（共 6 像素）；另有 2x2 实心方块变体... → 边框标记（矩形边的一段）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/3/code.py:28:#   - 原 solver 先取某颜色所有像素的 bbox，再检查四角是否存在 L 形锚点，由此判断是 TLBR 还是 TRBL 被标记。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/2/code.py:3:# Change: L 形 3 像素角标记，位于外接矩形的对角两端（共 6 像素）；另有 2x2 实心方块变体... → 线段标记（水平/垂直短线）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D8/0/code.py:3:# Change: 保留标记 — 标记 L 形角和图例在输出中保持不变... → 擦除标记（仅保留填充结果）\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D8/0/code.py:115:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D1/1/code.py:4:#         改为最短路径连接（含拐弯）——在同一对角线上的两个蓝色端点之间绘制固定规则的 L 形最短路。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D1/1/code.py:10:#   最后沿该列竖直走到较下方的端点。品红像素只有在这条 L 形主路径上时才触发。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D1/1/code.py:1